Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · array · mental-model · L1
Concept: An array parameter is really a pointer, so sizeof inside the function does not give the array size
Misconception: sizeof(a) / sizeof(a[0]) works on an array parameter.
Explanation: In a function parameter list int a[] means int *a. The array decays to a pointer to its first element, so sizeof(a) is the size of a pointer (8 bytes on 64-bit Linux) and the division gives 2, not the element count. The compiler warns with -Wsizeof-array-argument. Pass the length as a separate size_t parameter. sizeof only counts elements where the array is declared.
Incorrect (compiles with a warning: sizeof-array-argument):
size_t countBad(int a[]) {
  return sizeof(a) / sizeof(a[0]);
}
Correct:
size_t sumInts(const int *a, size_t n) {
  size_t s = 0;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) s += (size_t)a[i];
  return s;
}
Complexity: O(1)

