Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · AVL trees · transformation · L3
Concept: After a rotation update the heights bottom-up: the demoted node first, then the new root
Misconception: The two nodes' heights can be updated in either order.
Explanation: A right rotation lifts the left child x above y and moves x's right subtree under y. The new height of x depends on the height of y, so y must be updated first. Updating x first uses y's stale height and leaves a wrong value that later balance factors trust. Rotations are O(1) and keep the inorder order.
Incorrect:
typedef struct ANode { int key, h; struct ANode *l, *r; } ANode;
ANode *rotRBad(ANode *y) {
  ANode *x = y->l;
  y->l = x->r;
  x->r = y;
  aupd(x);
  aupd(y);
  return x;
}
Correct:
typedef struct ANode { int key, h; struct ANode *l, *r; } ANode;
ANode *rotR(ANode *y) {
  ANode *x = y->l;
  y->l = x->r;
  x->r = y;
  aupd(y);
  aupd(x);
  return x;
}
ANode *rotL(ANode *x) {
  ANode *y = x->r;
  x->r = y->l;
  y->l = x;
  aupd(x);
  aupd(y);
  return y;
}
Complexity: O(1)

