Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · Bloom filters · access · L3
Concept: Add sets all k bits; a key is possibly present only if all k bits are set, and never a false negative
Misconception: A key is present if any of its k bits is set.
Explanation: Membership needs all k bits. Checking for any set bit reports a key as present as soon as it shares one bit with something else, which inflates the false-positive rate far above the design value. A Bloom filter can answer definitely not present or possibly present: an added key always has all its bits set, so there are no false negatives. Add and query are O(k).
Incorrect:
int queryAnyBad(const uint32_t *w, const size_t *idx, unsigned k) {
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < k; i++)
    if ((w[idx[i] / 32] >> (idx[i] % 32)) & 1u) return 1;
  return 0;
}
Correct:
void bloomAdd(Bloom *b, const char *key) {
  uint64_t h1 = bloomH1(key), h2 = bloomH2(key);
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < b->k; i++) bitSet(b->w, bloomProbe(h1, h2, i, b->m));
}
int bloomMaybe(const Bloom *b, const char *key) {
  uint64_t h1 = bloomH1(key), h2 = bloomH2(key);
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < b->k; i++)
    if (!bitGet(b->w, bloomProbe(h1, h2, i, b->m))) return 0;
  return 1;
}
Complexity: O(k)

