Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · disjoint sets (union-find) · mutation · L3
Concept: Decrement the component count only when the roots differ
Misconception: Every union call merges two components, so it can decrement the count.
Explanation: Joining two elements that are already in the same set changes nothing. A union that decrements the component count unconditionally drifts below the true number of components, and can even reach zero for a connected graph. Return whether a merge happened and decrement only then.
Incorrect:
int dsUnionCountBad(size_t *p, size_t *count, size_t a, size_t b) {
  while (p[a] != a) a = p[a];
  while (p[b] != b) b = p[b];
  p[a] = b;
  (*count)--;
  return 1;
}
Correct:
size_t dsComponents(const DSU *d) { return d->count; }
int dsConnected(DSU *d, size_t a, size_t b) {
  size_t ra = dsFind(d, a), rb = dsFind(d, b);
  return ra != DS_NONE && ra == rb;
}
Complexity: O(1)

