Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · dynamic memory buffers · mutation · L3
Concept: realloc may move the block: use the returned pointer and re-read old addresses by index
Misconception: A pointer into a buffer stays valid after realloc grows it.
Explanation: realloc may allocate a new block, copy the data and free the old one, so every pointer into the old block dangles. Keep indexes instead of element pointers across a growth. Assign the result to a temporary so the original pointer is not lost and leaked when realloc returns NULL.
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: heap-use-after-free):
int growKeepPtrBad(void) {
  int *p = malloc(4 * sizeof *p);
  p[0] = 7;
  int *first = p;
  int *q = realloc(p, 1000 * sizeof *q);
  int v = *first;
  free(q);
  return v;
}
Correct:
int growKeepIndex(void) {
  int *p = malloc(4 * sizeof *p);
  p[0] = 7;
  int *q = realloc(p, 1000 * sizeof *q);
  if (q == NULL) { free(p); return -1; }
  int v = q[0];
  free(q);
  return v;
}
Complexity: O(n)

