C · edge lists · ordering · L2
Concept: Sort edges by weight with a comparator that returns (a > b) - (a < b), not a - b
Misconception: A qsort comparator can return the difference of the two weights.
Explanation: qsort only needs the sign of the result, but a.w - b.w overflows int when the weights are far apart, for example INT_MAX and a negative number; signed overflow is undefined behaviour that UBSan reports. Compare with (a > b) - (a < b), which cannot overflow. Sorting is O(m log m).
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: signed integer overflow):
int edgeCmpBad(const void *a, const void *b) {
  return ((const Edge *)a)->w - ((const Edge *)b)->w;
}
Correct:
int edgeCmp(const void *a, const void *b) {
  const Edge *x = a, *y = b;
  return (x->w > y->w) - (x->w < y->w);
}
void elSort(EdgeList *l) {
  if (l->m > 1) qsort(l->e, l->m, sizeof *l->e, edgeCmp);
}
Complexity: O(m log m)

