Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · Fenwick trees (binary indexed trees) · mutation · L2
Concept: A point update walks up with i += lowbit(i); walking down leaves the covering nodes stale
Misconception: A point update can walk down with i -= lowbit(i), like a query.
Explanation: The nodes that cover position i are found by repeatedly adding lowbit(i), until the index passes n. Subtracting instead visits the nodes that a prefix query uses, which do not contain position i, so later prefix sums are wrong. The indexes are 1-based: index 0 is not valid (lowbit(0) is 0 and the loop would never end). Update is O(log n).
Incorrect:
void fenAddBad(long long *t, size_t n, size_t i, long long d) {
  (void)n;
  for (; i > 0; i -= (i & (~i + 1))) t[i] += d;
}
Correct:
int fenInit(Fenwick *f, size_t n) {
  f->t = calloc(n + 1, sizeof *f->t);
  f->n = f->t != NULL ? n : 0;
  return f->t != NULL;
}
void fenFree(Fenwick *f) { free(f->t); f->t = NULL; f->n = 0; }
int fenAdd(Fenwick *f, size_t i, long long d) {
  if (i == 0 || i > f->n) return 0;
  for (; i <= f->n; i += lowbit(i)) f->t[i] += d;
  return 1;
}
Complexity: O(log n)

