C · function pointer · mutation · L2
Concept: Pass a void * context to callbacks instead of using global state
Misconception: A callback can keep its running total in a global variable.
Explanation: A callback with no extra argument can only communicate through globals, which are shared by every caller and break reentrancy and threads. Give the callback a void *ctx parameter and let the caller pass the address of its own state, as qsort_r and most C libraries do.
Incorrect:
int g_total;
void addGlobal(int v) { g_total += v; }
void forEachBad(const int *a, size_t n, void (*f)(int)) {
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) f(a[i]);
}
Correct:
typedef void (*Visit)(int, void *);
void addTo(int v, void *ctx) { *(int *)ctx += v; }
void forEach(const int *a, size_t n, Visit f, void *ctx) {
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) f(a[i], ctx);
}
Complexity: O(n)

