Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · binary heaps · mental-model · L1
Concept: With 0-based arrays the children of i are 2i + 1 and 2i + 2, and the parent is (i - 1) / 2
Misconception: The children of index i are 2i and 2i + 1.
Explanation: Those formulas are for 1-based heaps. In a C array that starts at 0 the root is index 0, its children are 1 and 2, and in general the children of i are 2i + 1 and 2i + 2. The parent of i > 0 is (i - 1) / 2. A min-heap keeps every parent no larger than its children, which puts the minimum at index 0; the array is a complete binary tree with no pointers.
Incorrect:
size_t hLeftBad(size_t i) { return 2 * i; }
size_t hParentBad(size_t i) { return i / 2; }
Correct:
size_t hParent(size_t i) { return (i - 1) / 2; }
size_t hLeft(size_t i) { return 2 * i + 1; }
size_t hRight(size_t i) { return 2 * i + 2; }
int isMinHeap(const int *a, size_t n) {
  for (size_t i = 1; i < n; i++)
    if (a[(i - 1) / 2] > a[i]) return 0;
  return 1;
}
Complexity: O(1)

