C · intbits · access · L1
Concept: Print fixed-width integers with the PRI macros; %d is only right for int
Misconception: printf("%d", x) works for any integer type.
Explanation: The conversion specifier must match the argument type. An int64_t is long on LP64 Linux and long long on Windows, so no single specifier is portable. <inttypes.h> defines PRId64, PRIu8 and friends; write printf("%" PRId64, x). The compiler warns with -Wformat when they differ.
Incorrect (compiles with a warning: format):
void printBad(int64_t x) {
  printf("%d\n", x);
}
Correct:
void printGood(int64_t x) {
  printf("%" PRId64 "\n", x);
}
Complexity: O(1)

