Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · queues · patterns · L3
Concept: Breadth-first search marks a vertex when it is enqueued, not when it is dequeued
Misconception: Marking vertices when they leave the queue is equivalent.
Explanation: If a vertex is marked only when dequeued, every neighbor that is still waiting can be enqueued again by other vertices, so the queue grows beyond n entries and overflows a queue sized n. Mark and record the distance at enqueue time, then each vertex enters the queue once: O(V + E) with an adjacency list and O(V^2) with a matrix.
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow):
void bfsDistBad(int n, const int *adj, int src, int *dist) {
  int *q = malloc((size_t)n * sizeof *q);
  int *done = calloc((size_t)n, sizeof *done);
  size_t head = 0, tail = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) dist[i] = -1;
  dist[src] = 0;
  q[tail++] = src;
  while (head < tail) {
    int u = q[head++];
    if (done[u]) continue;
    done[u] = 1;
    for (int v = 0; v < n; v++)
      if (adj[u * n + v] && !done[v]) {
        if (dist[v] < 0) dist[v] = dist[u] + 1;
        q[tail++] = v;
      }
  }
  free(q);
  free(done);
}
Correct:
void bfsDist(int n, const int *adj, int src, int *dist) {
  int *q = malloc((size_t)n * sizeof *q);
  size_t head = 0, tail = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) dist[i] = -1;
  if (q == NULL) return;
  dist[src] = 0;
  q[tail++] = src;
  while (head < tail) {
    int u = q[head++];
    for (int v = 0; v < n; v++)
      if (adj[u * n + v] && dist[v] < 0) {
        dist[v] = dist[u] + 1;
        q[tail++] = v;
      }
  }
  free(q);
}
Complexity: O(V^2)

