Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · queues · edge-cases · L2
Concept: With only head and tail indexes, full and empty look identical; keep a length or leave one slot free
Misconception: head == tail tells you whether the queue is empty.
Explanation: In a ring buffer with just a head and a tail index, head == tail both when no element is stored and when all slots are used. Keep a separate count (as Queue does) or sacrifice one slot so that full means (tail + 1) % cap == head.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { int *data; size_t head, tail, cap; } RingBad;
void ringPushBad(RingBad *r, int v) {
  r->data[r->tail] = v;
  r->tail = (r->tail + 1) % r->cap;
}
int ringEmptyBad(const RingBad *r) { return r->head == r->tail; }
Correct:
typedef struct { int *data; size_t head, len, cap; } Queue;
int queueEmpty(const Queue *q) { return q->len == 0; }
int queueFull(const Queue *q) { return q->len == q->cap; }
Complexity: O(1)

