Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · stacks · complexity · L3
Concept: Keep a parallel stack of running minimums to read the minimum in O(1) after any pop
Misconception: A single min variable tracks the minimum of the stack.
Explanation: A single variable is correct after pushes but wrong after the minimum is popped, because the previous minimum is lost. Store at each position the minimum of the elements up to that position. The minimum is then the top of the parallel array, and push, pop and min are all O(1) at the cost of O(n) extra space.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { int v[64]; size_t len; int min; } MinStackBad;
void msPushBad(MinStackBad *s, int x) {
  if (s->len == 0 || x < s->min) s->min = x;
  s->v[s->len++] = x;
}
int msPopBad(MinStackBad *s) { return s->v[--s->len]; }
Correct:
typedef struct { int v[64], m[64]; size_t len; } MinStack;
void msPush(MinStack *s, int x) {
  s->v[s->len] = x;
  s->m[s->len] = (s->len == 0 || x < s->m[s->len - 1]) ? x : s->m[s->len - 1];
  s->len++;
}
int msPop(MinStack *s) { return s->v[--s->len]; }
int msMin(const MinStack *s) { return s->m[s->len - 1]; }
Complexity: O(1)

