Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c
C · string · mental-model · L1
Concept: A C string is a char array ending in a zero byte; strlen counts to it and sizeof does not
Misconception: sizeof tells you the length of a string.
Explanation: A string is a sequence of chars ended by '\0'. strlen walks to the terminator in O(n) and does not count it. sizeof on an array counts every byte including the terminator, and sizeof on a char * parameter is just the pointer size.
Incorrect:
size_t lenBad(const char *s) { return sizeof(s); }
Correct:
size_t lenGood(const char *s) {
  size_t n = 0;
  while (s[n] != '\0') n++;
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(n)

