Concept: Typedef a fixed-width type once so the size is decided in one place
Misconception: unsigned long is always 32 bits.
Explanation: Built-in integer sizes vary by platform: unsigned long is 8 bytes on 64-bit Linux and 4 on 64-bit Windows. Define application types such as typedef uint32_t Id; on top of the stdint types, and a width change becomes a one-line edit that every use follows.
