Concept: Clear one output bit with PORTx &= ~(1 << bit), not with a bare mask
Misconception: PORTB &= (1 << PB5) clears bit PB5.
Explanation: AND with a mask keeps the bits that are 1 in the mask. (1 << PB5) is 0x20, so the AND keeps only PB5 and clears the other seven pins. To clear one bit, AND with the complement: ~(1 << PB5) is 0xDF in the low byte, which keeps seven pins and clears PB5.
Incorrect:
void ledOffBad(void) {
  PORTB &= (1 << PB5);
}
Correct:
void ledOn(void) {
  PORTB |= (1 << PB5);
}
void ledOff(void) {
  PORTB &= ~(1 << PB5);
}
Complexity: O(1)

