Embedded C · AVR_Bare_Metal · avr gpio registers · access · Intermediate
Concept: Read an input pin as 0 or 1 with (PINx >> bit) & 1
Misconception: PINB & (1 << bit) is a boolean 0 or 1 that can be compared with 1.
Explanation: PINB & (1 << bit) keeps the bit in place, so for bit 2 it is 0 or 4, and for bit 7 it is 0 or 128. Comparing that with 1 works only for bit 0. Shift the bit down to position 0 and mask with 1 to get a clean 0 or 1, or compare with != 0. Read PINx, not PORTx: PORTx holds what you wrote, PINx holds the pin level.
Incorrect:
uint8_t pinReadBad(uint8_t bit) {
  return PINB & (1 << bit);
}
Correct:
uint8_t pinRead(uint8_t bit) {
