Embedded C · AVR_Bare_Metal · avr usart spi and twi · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Initialise USART0 for 8N1 with the 16-bit baud register, then enable RX and TX
Misconception: Writing only UCSZ00 gives an 8-bit frame.
Explanation: The frame size is a 3-bit field: UCSZ01 and UCSZ00 together select 8 data bits (UCSZ02 in UCSR0B stays 0). Setting UCSZ00 alone selects 6 bits, so every byte is cut short. UBRR0 is a 16-bit register pair and avr-gcc writes it in the right order when you assign a 16-bit value. RXEN0 and TXEN0 in UCSR0B connect the pins.
Incorrect:
void uartInitBad(uint16_t u) {
  UBRR0 = u;
  UCSR0B = (1 << RXEN0) | (1 << TXEN0);
  UCSR0C = (1 << UCSZ00);
}
Correct:
void uartInit(uint16_t u, int u2x) {
  UBRR0 = u;
  if (u2x) UCSR0A |= (1 << U2X0); else UCSR0A &= ~(1 << U2X0);
  UCSR0B = (1 << RXEN0) | (1 << TXEN0);
  UCSR0C = (1 << UCSZ01) | (1 << UCSZ00);
}
Complexity: O(1)

