Embedded C · ESP_IDF · ble advertising and gatt · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Append an advertising data structure whose length byte counts the type byte and whose total stays within 31 bytes
Misconception: The length byte of an advertising structure holds the number of data bytes.
Explanation: An advertising packet carries at most 31 bytes of structures, each laid out as length, type and data. The length byte counts the type byte plus the data, so a 6-byte name has length 7. The flags structure 02 01 06 followed by the complete name "Sensor" gives 02 01 06 07 09 53 65 6E 73 6F 72, which is 11 bytes. The room check must include the 2 header bytes; leaving them out lets a long name write past byte 31.
Incorrect:
int adAddBad(uint8_t *b, int pos, uint8_t type, const void *d, uint8_t dl) {
  if (pos + dl > 31) return -1;
  b[pos] = dl;
  b[pos + 1] = type;
  memcpy(b + pos + 2, d, dl);
  return pos + 2 + dl;
}
Correct:
int adAdd(uint8_t *b, int pos, uint8_t type, const void *d, uint8_t dl) {
  if (pos + 2 + dl > 31) return -1;
  b[pos] = (uint8_t)(dl + 1U);
  b[pos + 1] = type;
  memcpy(b + pos + 2, d, dl);
  return pos + 2 + dl;
}
Complexity: O(n)

