Embedded C · ESP_IDF · ble advertising and gatt · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Validate connection parameters in their own units: interval 1.25 ms, timeout 10 ms, with the supervision rule
Misconception: The supervision timeout only has to be larger than the connection interval.
Explanation: The interval is counted in units of 1.25 ms (6 to 3200) and the supervision timeout in units of 10 ms (10 to 3200), so raw numbers cannot be compared. The timeout must exceed (1 + latency) x interval x 2, otherwise the link drops while the peripheral legitimately skips events. In integer units that is 4 x timeout > (1 + latency) x interval. Interval 800 (1 s) with latency 4 needs more than 10 s, so a 10 s timeout (1000) is rejected, although 1000 is larger than 800 as a raw number.
Incorrect:
int connBad(unsigned i, unsigned lat, unsigned t) {
  (void)lat;
  return i >= 6 && i <= 3200 && t >= 10 && t <= 3200 && t > i;
}
Correct:
int connOk(unsigned i, unsigned lat, unsigned t) {
  if (i < 6 || i > 3200 || t < 10 || t > 3200 || lat > 499) return 0;
  return 4U * t > (1U + lat) * i;
}
Complexity: O(1)

