Concept: Compute the notification payload size and packet count from the negotiated ATT MTU
Misconception: A notification can carry as many bytes as the MTU.
Explanation: An ATT notification spends 3 bytes on the opcode and the attribute handle, so the payload is MTU - 3. With the default MTU of 23 that is 20 bytes, and with an MTU of 247 it is 244. Sending 46 bytes at the default MTU takes ceil(46 / 20) = 3 notifications; dividing by the MTU itself says 2 and the stack truncates or rejects the oversized packets.
Incorrect:
unsigned packetsBad(unsigned n, unsigned mtu) { return (n + mtu - 1U) / mtu; }
Correct:
unsigned chunkLen(unsigned mtu) { return mtu - 3U; }
unsigned notifyPackets(unsigned n, unsigned mtu) {
  unsigned c = chunkLen(mtu);
  return (n + c - 1U) / c;
}
Complexity: O(1)

