Concept: Send a notification only when the characteristic allows it and the client has enabled it in the CCCD
Misconception: A characteristic with the notify property can notify at any time.
Explanation: The properties byte lists what a characteristic supports: read 0x02, write without response 0x04, write 0x08, notify 0x10 and indicate 0x20. Support is not permission. The client switches notifications on by writing 0x0001 to the client characteristic configuration descriptor (CCCD), and 0x0002 enables indications. Notifying before that write wastes airtime and a stack may return an error. Test the property bit and the CCCD bit together, with a bit test and not an equality test.
Incorrect:
int canNotifyBad(uint8_t props, uint16_t cccd) {
  (void)cccd;
  return (props & 0x10U) != 0;
}
Correct:
int canNotify(uint8_t props, uint16_t cccd) {
  return (props & 0x10U) != 0 && (cccd & 0x0001U) != 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

