Embedded C · STM32_HAL · can bus · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Build the identifier field of the transmit mailbox for standard and extended frames
Misconception: The identifier sits in the same bits for standard and extended frames.
Explanation: In the bxCAN transmit identifier register TIR a standard 11-bit identifier occupies bits 31 to 21. An extended 29-bit identifier occupies bits 31 to 3 and the IDE bit (bit 2) must be set. The RTR bit is bit 1 and the TXRQ request bit is bit 0. Using the standard shift for an extended frame cuts off the top 8 identifier bits and leaves IDE clear, so the frame goes out as a different, standard frame.
Incorrect:
uint32_t tirBad(uint32_t id, int ext) {
  (void)ext;
  return id << 21;
}
Correct:
uint32_t canTir(uint32_t id, int ext) {
  if (ext) return ((id & 0x1FFFFFFFU) << 3) | 4U;
  return (id & 0x7FFU) << 21;
}
Complexity: O(1)

