Embedded C · STM32_HAL · clock tree · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Encode M, N, P and Q into PLLCFGR with P as a two-bit code and the HSE source bit set
Misconception: The P field holds the divider value directly.
Explanation: PLLCFGR holds M in bits 5:0, N in bits 14:6, the P code in bits 17:16, the source select in bit 22 (1 for HSE) and Q in bits 27:24. The P field is a code, not a divider: 0 means 2, 1 means 4, 2 means 6 and 3 means 8, so P = (divider / 2) - 1. Writing the divider itself selects the wrong value.
Incorrect:
uint32_t cfgrBad(uint32_t m, uint32_t n, uint32_t p, uint32_t q) {
  return m | (n << 6) | (p << 16) | (1U << 22) | (q << 24);
}
Correct:
uint32_t pllcfgr(uint32_t m, uint32_t n, uint32_t p, uint32_t q) {
  uint32_t pc = ((p / 2U) - 1U) & 3U;
  return (m & 0x3FU) | ((n & 0x1FFU) << 6) | (pc << 16) | (1U << 22) | ((q & 0xFU) << 24);
}
Complexity: O(1)

