Embedded C · STM32_HAL · clock tree · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Pick the flash wait states for a core clock, rounding down at exact multiples of the step
Misconception: The number of wait states is the clock divided by 30 MHz.
Explanation: At 2.7 to 3.6 V the STM32F4 flash needs one more wait state for each 30 MHz step of the core clock: 0 wait states up to and including 30 MHz, 1 up to 60 MHz, and so on. The count is (hclk - 1) / 30 MHz; plain division gives one too many at exactly 30, 60, 90, 120, 150 and 180 MHz. The latency must be set before the clock is raised.
Incorrect:
uint32_t waitBad(uint32_t hclk) {
  return hclk / 30000000U;
}
Correct:
uint32_t flashWaits(uint32_t hclk) {
  return (hclk - 1U) / 30000000U;
}
Complexity: O(1)

