Embedded C · STM32_HAL · clock tree · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Switch to the PLL clock in a safe order: oscillator, PLL, flash latency, then the switch
Misconception: The system clock can be switched as soon as the PLL is ready; the flash settings can follow.
Explanation: Raising the clock before the flash has the right number of wait states makes the CPU read instructions that the flash cannot deliver in time. The safe order is: start the oscillator and wait for it, start the PLL and wait for it, set the flash latency (and bus prescalers), switch the clock source, and wait until the status confirms the switch. Each wait needs a timeout so a missing crystal does not hang start-up.
Incorrect:
void switchBad(void (*step)(int)) {
  step(1); step(2); step(4); step(3);
}
Correct:
void clockUp(void (*step)(int)) {
  step(1);
  step(2);
  step(3);
  step(4);
}
Complexity: O(1)

