Embedded C · STM32_HAL · crc calculation · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Compute the reflected CRC-32 used by Ethernet and zip with initial and final XOR
Misconception: CRC-32 starts at zero and ends with the raw register value.
Explanation: The common CRC-32 is reflected: it processes the low bit first with the reversed polynomial 0xEDB88320, starts the register at 0xFFFFFFFF and XORs the result with 0xFFFFFFFF at the end. The check value for 123456789 is 0xCBF43926. Skipping the initial value or the final XOR gives a valid-looking number that no other implementation will match.
Incorrect:
uint32_t crc32Bad(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint32_t crc = 0;
  while (n--) {
    crc ^= *p++;
    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) crc = (crc & 1U) ? (crc >> 1) ^ 0xEDB88320U : crc >> 1;
  }
  return crc;
}
Correct:
uint32_t crc32(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint32_t crc = 0xFFFFFFFFU;
  while (n--) {
    crc ^= *p++;
    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) crc = (crc & 1U) ? (crc >> 1) ^ 0xEDB88320U : crc >> 1;
  }
  return crc ^ 0xFFFFFFFFU;
}
Complexity: O(n)

