Embedded C · STM32_HAL · checksum · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Verify a received frame by summing all bytes including the checksum byte
Misconception: To verify a frame, recompute the checksum over all bytes and compare it with the last byte.
Explanation: With a two-complement checksum the receiver sums every byte of the frame including the checksum, and a good frame gives zero. A common mistake is to include the checksum byte in the calculation and then compare against it, which only matches by accident. Also check the length first, because an empty frame has no checksum byte to read.
Incorrect:
int verifyBad(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  return sum2c(p, n) == p[n - 1];
}
Correct:
int verify2c(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint8_t s = 0;
  if (n == 0) return 0;
  while (n--) s = (uint8_t)(s + *p++);
  return s == 0;
}
Complexity: O(n)

