Embedded C · Arduino_C · buttons and debouncing · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Report a press once, on the stable falling edge, not on every loop while held
Misconception: Acting whenever the button is pressed gives one action per press.
Explanation: loop() runs thousands of times per second, so a level test fires on every pass while the button is held. A press event is a transition: the stable level was HIGH on the previous pass and is LOW now. Keep the previous stable level and compare. The same idea gives a release event with the opposite change.
Incorrect:
int pressedCountBad(const uint8_t *stable, int n) {
  int count = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    if (stable[i] == 0) count++;
  return count;
}
Correct:
int pressEvent(uint8_t *prev, uint8_t stable) {
  int ev = (*prev == 1 && stable == 0);
  *prev = stable;
  return ev;
}
Complexity: O(1)

