Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: Arduino_C
Embedded C · Arduino_C · buttons and debouncing · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Tell a short press from a long press by comparing the hold time at release
Misconception: Calling delay(1000) and testing the pin again detects a long press.
Explanation: delay() freezes everything else for a second. Record the time at the press event and decide at the release event: a hold shorter than the long-press time is a short press, otherwise a long press. The decision uses only two timestamps, and the unsigned subtraction keeps it correct across a millis() wrap.
Incorrect:
int classifyBad(uint32_t t) {
  delay(1000);
  return t > 0;
}
Correct:
enum { PRESS_NONE, PRESS_SHORT, PRESS_LONG };
int classify(uint32_t pressedAt, uint32_t releasedAt, uint32_t longMs) {
  uint32_t held = (uint32_t)(releasedAt - pressedAt);
  if (held < 20U) return PRESS_NONE;
  return held >= longMs ? PRESS_LONG : PRESS_SHORT;
}
Complexity: O(1)

