Concept: Wire a button to ground, use INPUT_PULLUP and treat LOW as pressed
Misconception: A pressed button reads HIGH.
Explanation: With INPUT_PULLUP the internal resistor holds the pin HIGH while the button is open, and the button connects the pin to ground when pressed, so the pin reads LOW. No external resistor is needed and the pin never floats. The code must therefore invert the meaning: pressed means digitalRead(pin) == LOW.
Incorrect:
int pressedBad(uint8_t pin) {
  return digitalRead(pin) == HIGH;
}
Correct:
void buttonBegin(uint8_t pin) {
  pinMode(pin, INPUT_PULLUP);
}
int pressed(uint8_t pin) {
  return digitalRead(pin) == LOW;
}
Complexity: O(1)

