Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · dma · iteration · Advanced
Concept: Drain the circular buffer from tail to head, wrapping at the end of the buffer
Misconception: A drain loop that copies from tail up to head works for every position.
Explanation: If head is below tail the new data is in two pieces: from tail to the end of the buffer and from the start to head. Loop with an index that wraps (i = (i + 1) % size) until it reaches head, and store the new tail. A loop that only runs while i < head skips the first piece after a wrap.
Incorrect:
size_t drainBad(const uint8_t *buf, size_t size, size_t *tail, size_t head, uint8_t *out) {
  (void)size;
  size_t n = 0;
  for (size_t i = *tail; i < head; i++) out[n++] = buf[i];
  *tail = head;
  return n;
}
Correct:
size_t dmaDrain(const uint8_t *buf, size_t size, size_t *tail, size_t head, uint8_t *out) {
  size_t n = 0, i = *tail;
  while (i != head) { out[n++] = buf[i]; i = (i + 1) % size; }
  *tail = head;
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(n)

