Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · dma · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Track buffer ownership so the CPU does not touch a buffer while a transfer is running
Misconception: The CPU may fill the transmit buffer again as soon as the transfer has started.
Explanation: While DMA reads a transmit buffer, changing it corrupts the frame that is on the wire. Keep a busy flag that is set when the transfer starts and cleared in the transfer-complete interrupt, and refuse to write the buffer while it is set.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { uint8_t d[8]; volatile int busy; } TxBuf;
int fillBad(TxBuf *b, uint8_t v) {
  b->d[0] = v;
  return 0;
}
Correct:
typedef struct { uint8_t d[8]; volatile int busy; } TxBuf;
int txFill(TxBuf *b, uint8_t v) {
  if (b->busy) return -1;
  b->d[0] = v;
  return 0;
}
void txStart(TxBuf *b) { b->busy = 1; }
void txDone(TxBuf *b) { b->busy = 0; }
Complexity: O(1)

