Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · nvic and exti interrupts · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Handle every pending line in a shared handler such as EXTI9_5 with a loop over the PR bits
Misconception: EXTI9_5_IRQHandler can check the lines in an else-if chain.
Explanation: Lines 5 to 9 share one vector. If two pins trigger before the handler runs, an else-if chain handles only the first and the second pending bit makes the handler run again later, at the cost of latency and, if it was cleared by the wrong write, loss. Read PR once, loop over lines 5 to 9, call the handler for each set bit and acknowledge that bit.
Incorrect:
int dispatchBad(uint32_t pr, void (*h[10])(void)) {
  if (pr & (1U << 5)) { h[5](); return 1; }
  else if (pr & (1U << 6)) { h[6](); return 1; }
  return 0;
}
Correct:
int dispatch5to9(uint32_t pr, void (*h[10])(void)) {
  int n = 0;
  for (unsigned line = 5; line <= 9; line++) {
    if (pr & (1U << line)) {
      h[line]();
      EXTI->PR = 1U << line;
      n++;
    }
  }
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(1)

