Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · h-bridge motor driver · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Limit the speed change per update without overshooting the target
Misconception: Adding the step to the current speed moves it toward the target.
Explanation: A soft start limits the change per update so the supply and the mechanics are not shocked. Adding a fixed step can jump past the target when the remaining distance is smaller than the step, so the speed oscillates around it. Clamp the move to the remaining distance.
Incorrect:
int rampBad(int cur, int target, int step) {
  return cur < target ? cur + step : cur - step;
}
Correct:
int ramp(int cur, int target, int step) {
  if (cur < target) return cur + step > target ? target : cur + step;
  if (cur > target) return cur - step < target ? target : cur - step;
  return cur;
}
Complexity: O(1)

