Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c master · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Compute the largest pull-up resistor that meets the rise time for a given bus capacitance
Misconception: A 32-bit multiply is wide enough for the pull-up formula.
Explanation: The open-drain bus rises through the pull-up resistor Rp, so the 30 to 70 percent rise time is about 0.8473 x Rp x Cb. For a rise-time limit tr (1000 ns in standard mode, 300 ns in fast mode) the largest resistor is Rp = tr / (0.8473 x Cb). In integer arithmetic the numerator tr_ns x 10^7 reaches 10^10, which does not fit in 32 bits and silently wraps for unsigned values; use a 64-bit intermediate. Treat the result as an upper bound and check the lower bound from the sink current.
Incorrect:
uint32_t rpMaxBad(uint32_t trNs, uint32_t cbPf) {
  return trNs * 10000000U / (8473U * cbPf);
}
Correct:
uint32_t i2cRpMax(uint32_t trNs, uint32_t cbPf) {
  return (uint32_t)((uint64_t)trNs * 10000000ULL / (8473ULL * cbPf));
}
Complexity: O(1)

