Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c master · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Free a bus held low by a slave with up to nine clock pulses followed by a STOP
Misconception: One clock pulse is enough to release a stuck bus.
Explanation: If the microcontroller resets in the middle of a transfer, a slave may still be driving SDA low while it waits for the rest of a byte. The master cannot issue a START until SDA is released. Pulse SCL until SDA goes high, at most nine times (eight data bits and the acknowledge), and then create a STOP condition by pulling SDA low and releasing it while SCL is high. Give up and report an error after nine pulses.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { void (*scl)(int); void (*sdaOut)(int); int (*sda)(void); } I2cLines;
int recoverBad(const I2cLines *l) {
  l->scl(1);
  l->scl(0);
  l->scl(1);
  return l->sda() ? 1 : -1;
}
Correct:
typedef struct { void (*scl)(int); void (*sdaOut)(int); int (*sda)(void); } I2cLines;
int i2cRecover(const I2cLines *l) {
  int n = 0;
  l->sdaOut(1);
  l->scl(1);
  while (n < 9 && !l->sda()) { l->scl(0); l->scl(1); n++; }
  if (!l->sda()) return -1;
  l->scl(0); l->sdaOut(0); l->scl(1); l->sdaOut(1);
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(1)

