Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c master · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Scan the usable address range 0x08 to 0x77 and collect the devices that acknowledge
Misconception: A bus scan should probe every address from 0 to 127.
Explanation: I2C reserves addresses 0x00 to 0x07 (general call, START byte, CBUS, high-speed master code and others) and 0x78 to 0x7F (10-bit addressing and reserved). A scan probes only 0x08 to 0x77, which is 112 addresses. Use HAL_I2C_IsDeviceReady with one trial and a short timeout and store each address that answers.
Incorrect:
int scanBad(I2C_HandleTypeDef *h, uint8_t *found) {
  int n = 0;
  for (uint8_t a = 0; a < 128; a++)
    if (HAL_I2C_IsDeviceReady(h, i2cDev(a), 1, 2) == HAL_OK) found[n++] = a;
  return n;
}
Correct:
int i2cScan(I2C_HandleTypeDef *h, uint8_t *found) {
  int n = 0;
  for (uint8_t a = 0x08; a <= 0x77; a++)
    if (HAL_I2C_IsDeviceReady(h, i2cDev(a), 1, 2) == HAL_OK) found[n++] = a;
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(n)

