Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · lwip networking · patterns · Advanced
Concept: Compare TCP sequence numbers with modular arithmetic so that the wrap at 2^32 is handled
Misconception: Sequence number a comes before b when a < b.
Explanation: TCP sequence numbers are 32-bit and wrap around. The ordering is defined modulo 2^32: a is before b when the signed 32-bit difference a - b is negative, which is the TCP_SEQ_LT macro in lwIP. A plain a < b says that 0xFFFFFFF0 comes after 5, although 5 is only 21 bytes later in the stream. A window test uses the same idea: seq is inside the window when the unsigned distance from the window start is less than its length.
Incorrect:
int seqLtBad(uint32_t a, uint32_t b) { return a < b; }
Correct:
int seqLt(uint32_t a, uint32_t b) { return (int32_t)(a - b) < 0; }
int inWin(uint32_t seq, uint32_t base, uint32_t len) {
  return (uint32_t)(seq - base) < len;
}
Complexity: O(1)

