Concept: Build a QoS 0 PUBLISH whose remaining length counts the 2-byte topic length field
Misconception: The remaining length is the topic length plus the payload length.
Explanation: In a QoS 0 PUBLISH the remaining length covers everything after the fixed header: the 2-byte topic length, the topic and the payload. Topic "t/a" with payload "hi" gives 2 + 3 + 2 = 7 and the packet 30 07 00 03 74 2F 61 68 69. Leaving out the 2 makes the length too small, so the broker cuts the payload short and parses its tail as a new packet.
Incorrect:
int mqPublishBad(uint8_t *o, const char *topic, const void *pl, size_t plen) {
  size_t tl = strlen(topic);
  int n = 0;
  o[n++] = 0x30;
  n += mqEncLen((uint32_t)(tl + plen), o + n);
  o[n++] = (uint8_t)(tl >> 8); o[n++] = (uint8_t)(tl & 0xFFU);
  memcpy(o + n, topic, tl); n += (int)tl;
  memcpy(o + n, pl, plen); n += (int)plen;
  return n;
}
Correct:
int mqPublish(uint8_t *o, const char *topic, const void *pl, size_t plen) {
  size_t tl = strlen(topic);
  int n = 0;
  o[n++] = 0x30;
  n += mqEncLen((uint32_t)(2 + tl + plen), o + n);
  o[n++] = (uint8_t)(tl >> 8); o[n++] = (uint8_t)(tl & 0xFFU);
  memcpy(o + n, topic, tl); n += (int)tl;
  memcpy(o + n, pl, plen); n += (int)plen;
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(n)

