Embedded C · ESP_IDF · mqtt client · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Match a subscription filter with the + and # wildcards against a topic name
Misconception: A subscription matches a topic when the two strings are equal.
Explanation: A filter is compared level by level, with levels separated by a slash. + matches exactly one level, including an empty one, and # at the end matches the remaining levels; "a/#" also matches "a" itself. So "a/+/c" matches "a/b/c" but "a/+" does not match "a/b/c". An equality test never receives messages published to a more specific topic than the filter.
Incorrect:
int topicBad(const char *f, const char *t) { return strcmp(f, t) == 0; }
Correct:
int topicMatch(const char *f, const char *t) {
  for (;;) {
    if (*f == '#') return 1;
    if (*f == '+') {
      while (*t && *t != '/') t++;
      f++;
      if (*f == 0) return *t == 0;
      continue;
    }
    if (f[0] == '/' && f[1] == '#' && f[2] == 0 && *t == 0) return 1;
    if (*f != *t) return 0;
    if (*f == 0) return 1;
    f++; t++;
  }
}
Complexity: O(n)

