Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · mqtt client · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Encode the MQTT remaining length as a variable-length integer of 7 bits per byte
Misconception: The remaining length is a single byte holding the low 8 bits of the size.
Explanation: MQTT stores the remaining length in 1 to 4 bytes. Each byte carries 7 bits of the value, least significant group first, and bit 7 means that another byte follows. 127 is 7F, 128 is 80 01 and 321 is C1 02; the largest value, 268435455, takes four bytes. Writing one raw byte truncates any packet of 128 bytes or more, and the broker then reads the following bytes as the next packet.
Incorrect:
int mqEncBad(uint32_t v, uint8_t *o) { o[0] = (uint8_t)v; return 1; }
Correct:
int mqEncLen(uint32_t v, uint8_t *o) {
  int n = 0;
  do {
    uint8_t b = (uint8_t)(v & 0x7FU);
    v >>= 7;
    if (v) b |= 0x80U;
    o[n++] = b;
  } while (v && n < 4);
  return n;
}
int mqDecLen(const uint8_t *p, uint32_t *v) {
  uint32_t r = 0; int n = 0;
  do {
    r |= (uint32_t)(p[n] & 0x7FU) << (7 * n);
  } while ((p[n++] & 0x80U) && n < 4);
  *v = r;
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(1)

