Embedded C · STM32_HAL · oled display over spi · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Pull the data/command line low for commands and back high for data around each SPI transfer
Misconception: The D/C line only needs to be set once at start-up.
Explanation: In 4-wire SPI the SSD1306 uses a separate D/C pin to tell commands from display data. Set it low before command bytes and high before data bytes, and release chip select between the two phases. A driver that leaves D/C low after a command sends the frame data as commands, and the display shows garbage or reconfigures itself.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { void (*dc)(int); void (*xfer)(uint8_t); } OledIo;
void flushBad(const OledIo *io, const uint8_t *d, int n) {
  io->dc(0);
  io->xfer(0xAF);
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) io->xfer(d[i]);
}
Correct:
typedef struct { void (*dc)(int); void (*xfer)(uint8_t); } OledIo;
void oledFlush(const OledIo *io, const uint8_t *d, int n) {
  io->dc(0);
  io->xfer(0xAF);
  io->dc(1);
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) io->xfer(d[i]);
}
Complexity: O(n)

