Concept: Send the column and page address window with inclusive end values before the frame
Misconception: The end value of the address window is the number of columns or pages.
Explanation: The column address command 0x21 takes a start and an end column, and the page command 0x22 a start and an end page, both inclusive. For the full 128 x 64 screen the window is columns 0 to 127 and pages 0 to 7. Sending 128 and 8 as the end values is out of range and makes some controllers wrap or ignore the command.
Incorrect:
int windowBad(uint8_t *out) {
  const uint8_t c[6] = {0x21, 0, 128, 0x22, 0, 8};
  memcpy(out, c, 6);
  return 6;
}
Correct:
int oledWindow(uint8_t *out) {
  const uint8_t c[6] = {0x21, 0, 127, 0x22, 0, 7};
  memcpy(out, c, 6);
  return 6;
}
Complexity: O(1)

