Embedded C · STM32_HAL · packet parsing · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Read a 16-bit little-endian field from the payload only if it lies inside the received length
Misconception: The payload buffer always holds valid data up to its full size.
Explanation: The buffer has room for PMAX bytes but only len of them belong to the current frame; the rest are stale bytes from earlier frames. A field read must check offset + 2 <= len and return an error otherwise, instead of returning leftover data that looks valid.
Incorrect:
int fieldBad(const uint8_t *buf, uint8_t len, uint8_t off, uint16_t *v) {
  (void)len;
  *v = (uint16_t)(buf[off] | (buf[off + 1] << 8));
  return 0;
}
Correct:
int pktU16(const uint8_t *buf, uint8_t len, uint8_t off, uint16_t *v) {
  if ((unsigned)off + 2U > len) return -1;
  *v = (uint16_t)(buf[off] | (buf[off + 1] << 8));
  return 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

