Embedded C · STM32_HAL · packet parsing · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Drop a half-received frame after a silent gap using wrap-safe time subtraction
Misconception: A timeout can be tested by comparing the current time with last plus the limit.
Explanation: If a byte is lost the parser would wait for the rest of the frame forever, swallowing the start of the next one. Record the time of the last byte and reset the parser when the gap exceeds a limit. Subtract unsigned times (now - last) and compare the difference; the sum last + limit wraps around near the end of the 32-bit millisecond counter and then reports a timeout that has not happened.
Incorrect:
int timedOutBad(uint32_t now, uint32_t last, uint32_t limit) {
  return now > last + limit;
}
Correct:
int timedOut(uint32_t now, uint32_t last, uint32_t limit) {
  return (uint32_t)(now - last) > limit;
}
Complexity: O(1)

