Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · pwm timers · edge-cases · Intermediate
Concept: Convert a permille command to a compare value with rounding and clamp it to 100 percent
Misconception: Truncating the division is fine and values above 1000 permille cannot happen.
Explanation: Truncation always rounds down, so a small non-zero command can become 0 and the output never turns on. Add half the divisor before dividing to round to the nearest step. Commands come from control loops and can overshoot, so clamp the input before scaling: a compare value beyond ARR + 1 is harmless in hardware but hides the saturation from the rest of the program.
Incorrect:
uint32_t ccrTruncBad(uint32_t arr, uint32_t permille) {
  return (arr + 1U) * permille / 1000U;
}
Correct:
uint32_t pwmCcrPermille(uint32_t arr, uint32_t permille) {
  if (permille > 1000U) permille = 1000U;
  return ((arr + 1U) * permille + 500U) / 1000U;
}
Complexity: O(1)

