Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · reset and brown-out · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Keep a boot counter across soft resets with a magic number that validates the retained data
Misconception: A variable placed in a no-init section always holds the value it had before the reset.
Explanation: RAM in a no-init section is not cleared by the start-up code, so it survives a soft reset, but after a power-on it holds random bits. Store a magic number next to the data: if the magic is wrong the contents are garbage and must be initialised; if it is right the data is from the previous run.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { uint32_t magic, count; } Ret;
uint32_t bootBad(Ret *r) { return ++r->count; }
Correct:
typedef struct { uint32_t magic, count; } Ret;
uint32_t bootCount(Ret *r) {
  if (r->magic != 0xB007C0DEU) { r->magic = 0xB007C0DEU; r->count = 0; }
  return ++r->count;
}
Complexity: O(1)

