Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · reset and brown-out · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Calculate the supply voltage from an ADC reading of the internal reference
Misconception: The supply voltage is proportional to the ADC reading of the internal reference.
Explanation: The internal reference VREFINT is fixed (about 1.2 V), so when the supply drops the ADC code for it rises. The factory stores the code measured at 3.3 V. The supply is therefore 3300 x cal / reading in millivolts. Using reading / cal inverts the ratio and reports the supply rising when it falls.
Incorrect:
uint32_t vddBad(uint32_t cal, uint32_t reading) {
  return (uint32_t)((uint64_t)3300U * reading / cal);
}
Correct:
uint32_t vddMv(uint32_t cal, uint32_t reading) {
  if (reading == 0) return 0;
  return (uint32_t)((uint64_t)3300U * cal / reading);
}
Complexity: O(1)

