Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos queues · creation · Beginner
Concept: Create a queue whose item size is the size of the message struct, not of a pointer
Misconception: A queue stores whatever size of item the sender passes.
Explanation: A FreeRTOS queue copies items by value and every item has the size fixed at creation. If the queue is created with the size of a 32-bit pointer (4 bytes) but the senders pass a struct, only the first bytes of each struct are copied and the receiver gets a truncated message. Use sizeof of the message type and check the returned handle for NULL.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { uint32_t id; uint16_t val; } Msg;
QueueHandle_t newBad(int len) { return xQueueCreate(len, sizeof(uint32_t)); }
Correct:
typedef struct { uint32_t id; uint16_t val; } Msg;
QueueHandle_t newQueue(int len) { return xQueueCreate(len, sizeof(Msg)); }
Complexity: O(1)

