Concept: Keep only the newest sample in a one-item queue with xQueueOverwrite
Misconception: A one-item queue keeps the oldest sample when it is full.
Explanation: xQueueSend on a full one-item queue fails and keeps the old sample, so a slow consumer reads stale data. xQueueOverwrite replaces the stored item, which suits the latest value of a sensor. It is meant for queues of length one.
Incorrect:
int latestBad(QueueHandle_t q, int v) {
  return xQueueSend(q, &v, 0) == pdTRUE ? 0 : -1;
}
Correct:
int latestPut(QueueHandle_t q, int v) {
  return xQueueOverwrite(q, &v) == pdTRUE ? 0 : -1;
}
Complexity: O(1)

