Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos queues · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Send different message kinds through one queue with a type tag and a union
Misconception: The receiver can read any member of the message union.
Explanation: A union holds one member at a time, and reading another member reinterprets the same bytes. Put a type tag next to the union and let the handler read only the member that the tag names. The queue item size is the size of the whole struct, which is that of the largest member plus the tag.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { uint8_t type; union { int32_t i; float f; uint8_t b[4]; } u; } Ev;
int32_t valBad(const Ev *e) { return e->u.i; }
Correct:
typedef struct { uint8_t type; union { int32_t i; float f; uint8_t b[4]; } u; } Ev;
int32_t evValue(const Ev *e) {
  switch (e->type) {
  case 0: return e->u.i;
  case 1: return (int32_t)e->u.f;
  case 2: return e->u.b[0];
  default: return -1;
  }
}
Complexity: O(1)

