Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos queues · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Count dropped messages when the queue is full instead of ignoring the result of xQueueSend
Misconception: xQueueSend always stores the message.
Explanation: With a zero timeout xQueueSend returns errQUEUE_FULL (pdFALSE) when the queue is full and the message is lost. A producer that ignores the result loses data silently. Check the return value, count the drops, and report the count so the queue length or the consumer speed can be fixed.
Incorrect:
void sendBad(QueueHandle_t q, const Msg *m, unsigned *drops) {
  (void)drops;
  xQueueSend(q, m, 0);
}
Correct:
void sendCount(QueueHandle_t q, const Msg *m, unsigned *drops) {
  if (xQueueSend(q, m, 0) != pdTRUE) (*drops)++;
}
Complexity: O(1)

