Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos queues · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Size a queue for a burst from the producer and consumer rates
Misconception: A queue only needs to be as long as the burst.
Explanation: During a burst of B messages arriving at rate in while the consumer removes messages at rate out, the queue fills at the difference of the rates. The required length is B minus the number the consumer takes during the burst, B x out / in, rounded up. A consumer as fast as the producer needs a length of one. Using B directly wastes RAM and hides a slow consumer.
Incorrect:
unsigned qLenBad(unsigned burst, unsigned inHz, unsigned outHz) {
  (void)inHz; (void)outHz;
  return burst;
}
Correct:
unsigned qLen(unsigned burst, unsigned inHz, unsigned outHz) {
  if (outHz >= inHz) return 1;
  unsigned drained = (unsigned)((uint64_t)burst * outHz / inHz);
  return burst - drained;
}
Complexity: O(1)

