Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos semaphores and mutexes · transformation · Advanced
Concept: Raise the owner priority to that of a waiting task so a medium-priority task cannot starve the owner
Misconception: A low-priority task holding a mutex cannot delay a high-priority task that waits for it.
Explanation: If a low-priority task holds a mutex that a high-priority task needs, a medium-priority task can preempt the owner and keep it from releasing the mutex, which delays the high-priority task for as long as the medium task runs: priority inversion. FreeRTOS mutexes use priority inheritance: the owner runs at the priority of the highest waiter until it gives the mutex back.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { int held, ownerBase, ownerEff; } Mx;
void waitBad(Mx *m, int prio) {
  (void)prio; (void)m;
}
Correct:
typedef struct { int held, ownerBase, ownerEff; } Mx;
void waitInherit(Mx *m, int prio) {
  if (m->held && prio > m->ownerEff) m->ownerEff = prio;
}
int canPreempt(const Mx *m, int prio) { return prio > m->ownerEff; }
Complexity: O(1)

