Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos tasks · creation · Beginner
Concept: Create a FreeRTOS task and check that xTaskCreate returned pdPASS
Misconception: xTaskCreate always succeeds.
Explanation: xTaskCreate allocates the task control block and the stack from the heap. It returns pdPASS on success and an error code (errCOULD_NOT_ALLOCATE_REQUIRED_MEMORY) when memory is short or a static limit is reached. A task that was never created never runs, so the caller must check the result. In ESP-IDF the stack size is in bytes; in vanilla FreeRTOS it is in words.
Incorrect:
typedef void (*TaskFn)(void *);
int startBad(TaskFn fn, UBaseType_t prio, TaskHandle_t *h) {
  xTaskCreate(fn, "worker", 2048, NULL, prio, h);
  return 0;
}
Correct:
typedef void (*TaskFn)(void *);
int startWorker(TaskFn fn, UBaseType_t prio, TaskHandle_t *h) {
  if (xTaskCreate(fn, "worker", 2048, NULL, prio, h) != pdPASS) return -1;
  return 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

