Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos tasks · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Pick the highest-priority ready task and share the time between equal priorities
Misconception: Among ready tasks the scheduler always runs the first one with the highest priority.
Explanation: FreeRTOS runs the ready task with the highest priority. Tasks of equal priority are time-sliced in turn, so one of them cannot starve the others. A pick function that always takes the first of the equal-priority tasks starves the rest. Continue the search after the task that ran last.
Incorrect:
int pickBad(const uint8_t *prio, const uint8_t *ready, int n, int last) {
  int best = -1;
  (void)last;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    if (ready[i] && (best < 0 || prio[i] > prio[best])) best = i;
  return best;
}
Correct:
int pickNext(const uint8_t *prio, const uint8_t *ready, int n, int last) {
  int best = -1;
  for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {
    int i = (last + k) % n;
    if (ready[i] && (best < 0 || prio[i] > prio[best])) best = i;
  }
  return best;
}
Complexity: O(n)

