Embedded C · STM32_HAL · static allocation · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Test for a power-of-two buffer size so index wrap can use a mask
Misconception: The test x & (x - 1) == 0 detects powers of two for every x.
Explanation: A power of two has exactly one bit set, and x & (x - 1) clears the lowest set bit, so the result is zero only for powers of two. Zero also gives zero, so the test must reject zero explicitly. A static size check like _Static_assert((N & (N - 1)) == 0, ...) stops a wrong buffer size at compile time.
Incorrect:
int pow2Bad(uint32_t x) {
  return (x & (x - 1U)) == 0;
}
Correct:
int isPow2(uint32_t x) {
  return x != 0 && (x & (x - 1U)) == 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

