Embedded C · STM32_HAL · sleep modes · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Estimate average current and battery life from the active and sleep currents and the duty cycle
Misconception: The average current is the mean of the active and sleep currents.
Explanation: A duty-cycled device spends most of its time asleep, so the average is weighted by time: (active current x active time + sleep current x sleep time) / period. A device that is active 50 ms in every second at 10 mA and sleeps at 5 microamps averages about 505 microamps, not 5 mA. Battery life in hours is capacity in microamp-hours divided by the average current in microamps; ignore self-discharge and temperature at this level.
Incorrect:
uint32_t avgBad(uint32_t actUa, uint32_t actMs, uint32_t slpUa, uint32_t perMs) {
  (void)actMs; (void)perMs;
  return (actUa + slpUa) / 2U;
}
Correct:
uint32_t avgUa(uint32_t actUa, uint32_t actMs, uint32_t slpUa, uint32_t perMs) {
  uint64_t q = (uint64_t)actUa * actMs + (uint64_t)slpUa * (perMs - actMs);
  return (uint32_t)(q / perMs);
}
uint32_t batteryHours(uint32_t mAh, uint32_t avg) { return avg ? mAh * 1000U / avg : 0; }
Complexity: O(1)

