Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · sleep modes · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Check the wake-up flag with interrupts masked so an interrupt cannot slip in before WFI
Misconception: Test the flag and then execute WFI; the interrupt will wake the CPU.
Explanation: If an interrupt sets the flag after the test but before WFI, the CPU goes to sleep with the flag already set and waits for the next unrelated interrupt. Mask interrupts, test the flag, execute WFI and unmask. WFI still wakes on a pending interrupt even when PRIMASK is set, so the masked interrupt is taken as soon as interrupts are enabled.
Incorrect:
int sleepRaceBad(volatile int *flag, void (*isr)(void)) {
  int missed = 0;
  if (!*flag) {
    isr();
    missed = *flag;
    __WFI();
  }
  return missed;
}
Correct:
int sleepWait(volatile int *flag, void (*isr)(void)) {
  int missed = 0;
  __disable_irq();
  if (!*flag) {
    isr();
    missed = *flag;
    __WFI();
  }
  __enable_irq();
  return missed;
}
Complexity: O(1)

