Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · sleep modes · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Enter Stop mode by clearing PDDS, clearing the wake-up flag and setting SLEEPDEEP
Misconception: Setting SLEEPDEEP and executing WFI is enough to enter Stop mode.
Explanation: In the STM32F4 power controller PDDS chooses what the deep mode is: 0 selects Stop (RAM and registers are kept), 1 selects Standby (RAM is lost and the part resets on wake-up). Clear PDDS, clear the wake-up flag with CWUF, set SLEEPDEEP, then WFI. After wake-up from Stop the system clock is back on the internal oscillator, so clear SLEEPDEEP again and restore the clock tree.
Incorrect:
void stopBad(void) {
  PWR->CR |= PWR_CR_PDDS;
  SCB->SCR |= SCB_SCR_SLEEPDEEP;
  __WFI();
}
Correct:
void stopEnter(void) {
  PWR->CR &= ~PWR_CR_PDDS;
  PWR->CR |= PWR_CR_CWUF;
  SCB->SCR |= SCB_SCR_SLEEPDEEP;
  __WFI();
  SCB->SCR &= ~SCB_SCR_SLEEPDEEP;
}
Complexity: O(1)

