Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · sleep modes · mental-model · Intermediate
Concept: Select Sleep or Stop by writing SLEEPDEEP explicitly before executing WFI
Misconception: WFI always enters the same low-power state.
Explanation: On a Cortex-M core WFI (wait for interrupt) stops the CPU clock until an interrupt becomes pending. Which state it enters depends on the SLEEPDEEP bit in SCB->SCR: clear gives Sleep (peripherals keep running), set gives the deep mode selected in the power controller. A routine that assumes the bit is clear goes into deep sleep, and loses its fast peripherals, when an earlier part of the code left it set.
Incorrect:
void sleepBad(void) {
  __WFI();
}
Correct:
void sleepShallow(void) {
  SCB->SCR &= ~SCB_SCR_SLEEPDEEP;
  __WFI();
}
Complexity: O(1)

