Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c sensor drivers · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Verify the chip identification register at start-up before using a sensor
Misconception: If the I2C transfer succeeds the right sensor is connected.
Explanation: A transfer succeeds whenever any device acknowledges the address, so a different chip on the same address, a clone or a wrong part number also gives HAL_OK. Read the identification register (WHO_AM_I, 0x75 on the MPU-6050 family, which reads 0x68) and compare it with the value from the datasheet. Return an error for both a failed transfer and a wrong identity.
Incorrect:
int sensorBad(I2C_HandleTypeDef *h, uint8_t a7) {
  uint8_t id;
  return HAL_I2C_Mem_Read(h, (uint16_t)(a7 << 1), 0x75,
                          I2C_MEMADD_SIZE_8BIT, &id, 1, 10) == HAL_OK ? 0 : -1;
}
Correct:
int sensorInit(I2C_HandleTypeDef *h, uint8_t a7) {
  uint8_t id = 0;
  if (HAL_I2C_Mem_Read(h, (uint16_t)(a7 << 1), 0x75,
                       I2C_MEMADD_SIZE_8BIT, &id, 1, 10) != HAL_OK) return -1;
  return id == 0x68 ? 0 : -2;
}
Complexity: O(1)

