Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c sensor drivers · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Scale raw acceleration counts to milli-g with the sensitivity of the selected range
Misconception: Dividing the raw count by the sensitivity first and then multiplying keeps the precision.
Explanation: The sensitivity is 16384 counts per g in the plus or minus 2 g range, 8192 at 4 g, 4096 at 8 g and 2048 at 16 g. Integer division of the raw count by 16384 before multiplying by 1000 throws the fraction away, so every reading below 1 g comes out as zero. Multiply first and then divide.
Incorrect:
int mgBad(int16_t raw, int lsbPerG) {
  return raw / lsbPerG * 1000;
}
Correct:
int milliG(int16_t raw, int lsbPerG) {
  return (int)((int32_t)raw * 1000 / lsbPerG);
}
int lsbPerG(int rangeG) {
  switch (rangeG) {
  case 2: return 16384;
  case 4: return 8192;
  case 8: return 4096;
  case 16: return 2048;
  default: return 0;
  }
}
Complexity: O(1)

