Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · servo and stepper motors · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Plan an acceleration ramp from the step rate and the acceleration, and convert the rate to a step delay
Misconception: The distance needed to reach a speed is the speed divided by the acceleration.
Explanation: With a constant acceleration a (steps per second squared) the stepper needs v squared divided by 2a steps to reach speed v (steps per second). Reaching 1000 steps/s at 2000 steps/s squared needs 250 steps, not 1000 / 2000 of a step. The delay between steps is one million microseconds divided by the rate. Starting at full speed without a ramp stalls the motor.
Incorrect:
uint32_t accelBad(uint32_t v, uint32_t a) {
  return v / a;
}
Correct:
uint32_t accelSteps(uint32_t v, uint32_t a) {
  return (uint32_t)((uint64_t)v * v / (2ULL * a));
}
uint32_t stepDelayUs(uint32_t sps) { return 1000000U / sps; }
Complexity: O(1)

