Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · structs and unions · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Compare structs member by member because padding bytes are indeterminate
Misconception: Two structs with equal members compare equal with memcmp.
Explanation: Padding bytes between members have no defined value, so memcmp on two structs with identical members can report a difference. Compare each member, or define a canonical byte form and compare that. The same applies to computing a CRC over a struct in memory: serialise first.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { uint8_t a; uint32_t b; } Pair;
int pairEqBad(const Pair *x, const Pair *y) {
  return memcmp(x, y, sizeof *x) == 0;
}
Correct:
typedef struct { uint8_t a; uint32_t b; } Pair;
int pairEq(const Pair *x, const Pair *y) {
  return x->a == y->a && x->b == y->b;
}
Complexity: O(1)

