Concept: Convert a servo angle from 0 to 180 degrees into a pulse width from 1000 to 2000 microseconds
Misconception: Divide the angle by 180 first to get the fraction of the range.
Explanation: A hobby servo reads a pulse every 20 ms and the pulse width sets the angle: about 1000 microseconds for 0 degrees, 1500 for 90 and 2000 for 180. In integer arithmetic multiply first: 1000 + angle x 1000 / 180. Dividing the angle by 180 first gives zero for every angle below 180.
Incorrect:
int usBad(int angle) {
  return 1000 + angle / 180 * 1000;
}
Correct:
int servoUs(int angle) {
  if (angle < 0) angle = 0;
  if (angle > 180) angle = 180;
  return 1000 + angle * 1000 / 180;
}
Complexity: O(1)

