Embedded C · STM32_HAL · hardware timers · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Start a periodic update interrupt: load PSC and ARR, enable UIE, enable the NVIC line, then CEN
Misconception: Setting CEN is enough to get an interrupt every period.
Explanation: The update interrupt needs three enables: UIE in DIER (the timer raises the request), the NVIC line for the timer (the core accepts it) and CEN in CR1 (the counter runs). An update event (UG) loads the buffered PSC and ARR first, and it sets UIF, so clear UIF before enabling the interrupt or the handler runs once immediately.
Incorrect:
void timerStartBad(TIM_TypeDef *t) {
  t->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;
}
Correct:
void timer2Start(uint32_t psc, uint32_t arr) {
  TIM2->PSC = psc;
  TIM2->ARR = arr;
  TIM2->EGR = TIM_EGR_UG;
  TIM2->SR = ~TIM_SR_UIF;
  TIM2->DIER |= TIM_DIER_UIE;
  NVIC_EnableIRQ(TIM2_IRQn);
  TIM2->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;
}
Complexity: O(1)

