Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · uart and usart · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Drive transmission from the TXE interrupt and switch the interrupt off when the buffer is empty
Misconception: Leave the TXE interrupt enabled so every new byte is sent automatically.
Explanation: TXE stays 1 whenever the data register is empty, so with TXEIE enabled and no data to send the interrupt fires again and again and the CPU does nothing else. The main code pushes bytes into a ring buffer and sets TXEIE; the handler sends the next byte, or clears TXEIE when the buffer is empty.
Incorrect:
void txIsrBad(uint8_t *buf, uint8_t *head, uint8_t *tail) {
  if (*head != *tail) USART2->DR = buf[(*tail)++ & 15];
}
Correct:
static uint8_t txBuf[16];
static volatile uint8_t txHead, txTail;
void uartPut(uint8_t b) {
  txBuf[txHead++ & 15U] = b;
  USART2->CR1 |= USART_CR1_TXEIE;
}
void USART2_IRQHandler(void) {
  if (USART2->SR & USART_SR_TXE) {
    if (txHead != txTail) USART2->DR = txBuf[txTail++ & 15U];
    else USART2->CR1 &= ~USART_CR1_TXEIE;
  }
}
Complexity: O(1)

