Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: c; platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · watchdog timers · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Feed the watchdog from the main loop only when every task has checked in
Misconception: Reloading the watchdog from a timer interrupt keeps the system safe.
Explanation: A timer interrupt keeps running even when the main loop is stuck, so feeding from it hides exactly the fault the watchdog exists to catch. Give each task a bit in a health word, set the bit when the task completes a cycle, and reload only when all bits are set; then clear the word. A task that stops reporting lets the watchdog expire and reset the system.
Incorrect:
void feedBad(void) {
  IWDG->KR = 0xAAAA;
}
Correct:
int wdtFeedIfHealthy(uint32_t *health, uint32_t all) {
  if (*health != all) return 0;
  IWDG->KR = 0xAAAA;
  *health = 0;
  return 1;
}
Complexity: O(1)

