Concept: Estimate the time to send a frame, which sets the maximum refresh rate
Misconception: Each LED takes 8 bit times in the frame.
Explanation: Each LED needs 24 bits of 1.25 microseconds, which is 30 microseconds, plus the reset gap once per frame. 60 LEDs take 1800 microseconds plus 280, about 2.1 milliseconds, so the refresh rate cannot exceed about 480 frames per second. Counting only 8 bits per LED underestimates the time threefold.
Incorrect:
uint32_t frameBad(uint32_t n, uint32_t resetUs) {
  return n * 10U + resetUs;
}
Correct:
uint32_t frameUs(uint32_t n, uint32_t resetUs) {
  return n * 30U + resetUs;
}
Complexity: O(1)

