Concept: Real-time clock chips store time as BCD, with a decimal digit in each nibble
Misconception: The byte 0x59 means 89 seconds.
Explanation: In binary-coded decimal the high nibble is the tens digit and the low nibble the ones digit, so 0x59 is 59, not 89. Convert with (b >> 4) * 10 + (b & 0x0F) and back with ((n // 10) << 4) | (n % 10). Parsing it as a normal integer gives out-of-range minutes and seconds.
Incorrect:
def bcd_bad(b):
    return b
Correct:
def bcd_to_int(b):
    return (b >> 4) * 10 + (b & 0x0F)
def int_to_bcd(n):
    return ((n // 10) << 4) | (n % 10)
Complexity: O(1)

