Concept: Extract a bit field by shifting right and then masking with width ones
Misconception: Masking first and shifting later gives the field value.
Explanation: To read width bits that start at bit shift, shift the register right by shift and then mask with (1 << width) - 1. Masking first leaves the bits in place, so the result is multiplied by 2 to the power shift. Writing a field is the reverse: clear the field, then OR in the shifted value.
