Explanation: Python lists accept negative indexes: grid[-1] is the last row. A neighbour at row -1 therefore reads a real cell on the opposite edge, silently joining the top and bottom of the grid, and IndexError appears only for indexes below -len. Check both ends: 0 <= r < rows and 0 <= c < cols.
