Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: ruby
Ruby · graphs stored as adjacency matrices · creation · L1
Concept: Build the rows with a block; Array.new(n, Array.new(n, 0)) makes every row the same object
Misconception: Array.new(n, Array.new(n, 0)) creates an n by n matrix of zeros.
Explanation: The second argument is evaluated once, so all n rows are references to one Array. Setting m[0][1] = 1 then appears in every row. The block form Array.new(n) { Array.new(n, 0) } runs the block for each row and gives each its own Array. The matrix needs O(V squared) space whatever the number of edges.
Incorrect:
def make_bad(n)
  Array.new(n, Array.new(n, 0))
end
Correct:
class MatrixGraph
  attr_reader :matrix, :size
  def initialize(n, directed: false)
    @size = n
    @directed = directed
    @matrix = Array.new(n) { Array.new(n, 0) }
  end
  def add_edge(u, v, weight = 1)
    @matrix[u][v] = weight
    @matrix[v][u] = weight unless @directed
    self
  end
  def edge?(u, v)
    @matrix[u][v] != 0
  end
  def neighbors(v)
    (0...@size).select { |u| @matrix[v][u] != 0 }
  end
end
Complexity: O(V^2)

