Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: ruby
Ruby · deques · mutation · L3
Concept: When a ring buffer grows it must copy elements in logical order, not physical order
Misconception: Appending empty slots to the buffer is enough to double the capacity.
Explanation: If the contents have wrapped around, extending the Array leaves the head and tail in the middle of the old region, and reading from head crosses empty slots. Copy the elements in logical order into a bigger buffer and reset head to 0. Growth costs O(n) but happens rarely, so push is O(1) amortised.
Incorrect:
class GrowBad
  def initialize(cap)
    @buf = Array.new(cap)
    @head = 0
    @size = 0
  end
  def push_back(v)
    @buf.concat(Array.new(@buf.size)) if @size == @buf.size
    @buf[(@head + @size) % @buf.size] = v
    @size += 1
  end
  def pop_front
    v = @buf[@head]
    @head = (@head + 1) % @buf.size
    @size -= 1
    v
  end
  def to_a
    Array.new(@size) { |i| @buf[(@head + i) % @buf.size] }
  end
end
Correct:
class AutoDeque < RingDeque
  def push_back(v)
    grow! if full?
    super
  end
  def push_front(v)
    grow! if full?
    super
  end
  private
  def grow!
    items = to_a
    @buf = items + Array.new([items.size, 1].max)
    @head = 0
  end
end
Complexity: O(1) amortised

