4.4 Algorithm chunks
A range query returns a whole node only when its range is inside the query, and zero when it
is outside
ts-segmenttree-query   lens: access   level: L2   family: ts-seg-access
Prerequisites: ts-segmenttree-build. Follow-up: ts-segmenttree-update. Complexity: O(log n).
 Common misconception. Return the node value whenever its range overlaps the query.
A node can be used as is only when its range lies completely inside the query range. When it partly overlaps, the
query must descend into both children. Returning the node on any overlap includes elements outside the query.
Ranges fully outside contribute the identity, which is 0 for a sum.
Incorrect (runs, but fails as described):
 function queryBad(
  t: SegTree, ql: number, qr: number, node = 1, l = 0, r = t.n - 1,
): number {
  if (qr < l || r < ql) return 0;
  return t.tree[node] as number;
}
Correct:
 function sumRange(
  t: SegTree, ql: number, qr: number, node = 1, l = 0, r = t.n - 1,
): number {
  if (qr < l || r < ql) return 0;
  if (ql <= l && r <= qr) return t.tree[node] as number;
  const mid = (l + r) >> 1;
  const left = sumRange(t, ql, qr, 2 * node, l, mid);
  return left + sumRange(t, ql, qr, 2 * node + 1, mid + 1, r);
}
A point update must recompute every ancestor on the way back up
ts-segmenttree-update   lens: mutation   level: L2   family: ts-seg-mutation
Prerequisites: ts-segmenttree-query. Follow-up: ts-segmenttree-min-identity. Complexity: O(log n).
 Common misconception. Writing the new value in the leaf is enough.
Ancestors store combined values. After changing a leaf, each node on the path to the root must be recomputed from
its children, which the recursion does after returning. Updating the leaf only leaves stale sums in every ancestor, so
any query that uses an ancestor is wrong.
Incorrect (runs, but fails as described):
 function updateBad(
  t: SegTree, i: number, v: number, node = 1, l = 0, r = t.n - 1,
): void {
  if (l === r) { t.tree[node] = v; return; }
  const mid = (l + r) >> 1;
  if (i <= mid) updateBad(t, i, v, 2 * node, l, mid);
  else updateBad(t, i, v, 2 * node + 1, mid + 1, r);
}

