Prompt. queryNoPush returns 0 for the range [0, 1] after rangeAdd(0, 3, 5) on a LazySeg of size 8. Why, and what is
the fix?
Answer key (mentor only, never embedded). rangeAdd stored the +5 on the node for [0, 3] as a pending tag and did
not update its children. queryNoPush descends into the children without pushing the tag, so it reads stale zeros. Push
the pending tag to both children before descending, as LazySeg.query does.
