2. Overview and mental model: Directed Graph
A directed graph is a set of vertices with one-way edges. The adjacency list stores, for each vertex, the list of vertices
it points to; it takes O(V + E) space.
Depth first search gives cycle detection and finishing orders; breadth first search gives shortest hop counts; Kahn's
algorithm gives topological order; Kosaraju groups strongly connected components.
Use directed graphs for dependencies, schedules, state machines and web links. For weighted edges see the
weighted graph document.
