TypeScript Deque: Training Data for the DSA Mentor RAG Chatbot
Page 3
A deque grows at both ends: pushFront must decrement the head before writing
ts-deque-core   lens: creation   level: L1   family: ts-deque-creation
Prerequisites: none. Follow-up: ts-deque-empty. Complexity: O(1).
 Common misconception. this.items.set(this.head--, x) inserts at the front.
The head index points at the first element, so a new front element goes one slot before it. Post-decrement writes at
the old head, overwriting the current first element and leaving the new head empty. Pre-decrement (--head) writes at
the new slot. A Map keyed by integer index, or a circular buffer, gives O(1) at both ends; Array.unshift is O(n).
Mnemonist (npm) has FixedDeque.
Incorrect (runs, but fails as described):
 class DequeBad<T> {
  private items = new Map<number, T>();
  private head = 0;
  private tail = 0;
  pushBack(x: T): void { this.items.set(this.tail++, x); }
  pushFront(x: T): void { this.items.set(this.head--, x); }
  toArray(): (T | undefined)[] {
    const out: (T | undefined)[] = [];
    for (let i = this.head; i < this.tail; i++) out.push(this.items.get(i));
    return out;
  }
}
Correct:
 class Deque<T> {
  private items = new Map<number, T>();
  private head = 0;
  private tail = 0;
  pushBack(x: T): void { this.items.set(this.tail++, x); }
  pushFront(x: T): void { this.items.set(--this.head, x); }
  popFront(): T | undefined {
    if (this.head === this.tail) return undefined;
    const x = this.items.get(this.head);
    this.items.delete(this.head++);
    return x;
  }
  popBack(): T | undefined {
    if (this.head === this.tail) return undefined;
    const x = this.items.get(--this.tail);
    this.items.delete(this.tail);
    return x;
  }
  peekFront(): T | undefined { return this.items.get(this.head); }
  peekBack(): T | undefined { return this.items.get(this.tail - 1); }
  get size(): number { return this.tail - this.head; }
  toArray(): T[] {
    const out: T[] = [];
    for (let i = this.head; i < this.tail; i++) out.push(this.items.get(i) as T);
    return out;
  }
}

