Sliding window maximum keeps a decreasing deque of indexes and drops the front when it
leaves the window
ts-deque-sliding-max   lens: patterns   level: L3   family: ts-deque-patterns
Prerequisites: ts-deque-rotate. Follow-up: ts-deque-zero-one-bfs. Complexity: O(n).
 Common misconception. Keeping a decreasing deque is enough; the front is always inside the window.
The deque holds indexes whose values decrease from front to back, so the front is the maximum. The front can be an
old index that has slid out of the window, and then it must be removed. Forgetting that check returns a stale
maximum. Each index is pushed and popped once: O(n).
Incorrect (runs, but fails as described):
 function maxSlidingBad(nums: number[], k: number): number[] {
  const dq = new Deque<number>();
  const out: number[] = [];
  nums.forEach((x, i) => {
    while (dq.size && (nums[dq.peekBack() as number] as number) <= x) dq.popBack();
    dq.pushBack(i);
    if (i >= k - 1) out.push(nums[dq.peekFront() as number] as number);
  });
  return out;
}
Correct:
 function maxSliding(nums: number[], k: number): number[] {
  const dq = new Deque<number>();
  const out: number[] = [];
  nums.forEach((x, i) => {
    if (dq.size && (dq.peekFront() as number) <= i - k) dq.popFront();
    while (dq.size && (nums[dq.peekBack() as number] as number) <= x) dq.popBack();
    dq.pushBack(i);
    if (i >= k - 1) out.push(nums[dq.peekFront() as number] as number);
  });
  return out;
}
0-1 BFS puts zero-weight neighbours at the front and must not mark a node final when it is
first reached
ts-deque-zero-one-bfs   lens: patterns   level: L3   family: ts-deque-patterns
Prerequisites: ts-deque-sliding-max. Follow-up: none. Complexity: O(V + E).
 Common misconception. Marking a node seen when it is first discovered gives shortest distances.
With edge weights 0 and 1 a node can be reached first by a weight-1 edge and later by a cheaper path of zero-weight
edges. Marking it seen on discovery freezes the worse distance. Use the distance array as the check (relax when
strictly better), pushFront for weight 0 and pushBack for weight 1. Total work stays O(V + E).

