TypeScript · binarytree · equality · L2
Concept: Two trees are equal when shape and values match; === compares object identity
Misconception: a === b tells whether two trees are the same.
Explanation: Objects are compared by reference. Two separately built trees with the same shape and values are not === equal. Compare structurally: both null, or both present with equal values and equal left and right subtrees.
Incorrect:
function isSameBad<T>(a: TreeNode<T> | null, b: TreeNode<T> | null): boolean {
  return a === b;
}
Correct:
function isSame<T>(a: TreeNode<T> | null, b: TreeNode<T> | null): boolean {
