Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · bst · ordering · L3
Concept: Floor keeps the best candidate seen so far; the last node visited may be larger than the query
Misconception: The floor of a key is the last node visited on the search path.
Explanation: The floor is the largest key that is at most the query. Moving right means the current node is a candidate, moving left means it is too large. The path may end on a node that is too large, so remember the best candidate in a variable and return it.
Incorrect:
function floorBad<K>(n: BNode<K> | null, key: K, cmp: Cmp<K>): K | null {
  let cur = n;
  let last: K | null = null;
  while (cur !== null) {
    last = cur.key;
    cur = cmp(key, cur.key) < 0 ? cur.left : cur.right;
  }
  return last;
}
Correct:
function floor<K>(n: BNode<K> | null, key: K, cmp: Cmp<K>): K | null {
  let cur = n;
  let best: K | null = null;
  while (cur !== null) {
    const c = cmp(key, cur.key);
    if (c === 0) return cur.key;
    if (c < 0) cur = cur.left;
    else { best = cur.key; cur = cur.right; }
  }
  return best;
}
Complexity: O(h)

