Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · bst · patterns · L3
Concept: Validate with lower and upper bounds that every node inherits, not only the parent comparison
Misconception: A tree is a BST if every node is greater than its left child and smaller than its right child.
Explanation: Comparing a node with its direct children misses violations deeper down: a key in the left subtree must be smaller than every ancestor on the path where the subtree hangs to the left. Pass the allowed open interval down the recursion and tighten it at each step.
Incorrect:
function isBstLocal(n: BNode<number> | null): boolean {
  if (n === null) return true;
  if (n.left !== null && n.left.key >= n.key) return false;
  if (n.right !== null && n.right.key <= n.key) return false;
  return isBstLocal(n.left) && isBstLocal(n.right);
}
Correct:
function isBst(
  n: BNode<number> | null, lo: number | null = null, hi: number | null = null,
): boolean {
  if (n === null) return true;
  if (lo !== null && n.key <= lo) return false;
  if (hi !== null && n.key >= hi) return false;
  return isBst(n.left, lo, n.key) && isBst(n.right, n.key, hi);
}
Complexity: O(n)

