Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · btree · insertion-and-deletion · L2
Concept: A full root is split under a new root; this is the only way the tree gets taller
Misconception: Insert into the root even when it is full.
Explanation: A full root has no parent to receive its median. Create a new empty root, make the old root its only child, split that child, and then insert. Skipping this step lets the root grow past 2t-1 keys. Height increases only here, at the top, so all leaves stay at the same depth.
Incorrect:
function insertNoGrow(tree: BTree, k: number): void {
  tree.insertNonFull(tree.root, k);
}
Correct:
class BTree {
  root = new BNode(true);
  constructor(readonly t: number) {}
  has(k: number): boolean { return search(this.root, k); }
  insert(k: number): void {
    if (this.has(k)) return;
    if (this.root.keys.length === 2 * this.t - 1) {
      const s = new BNode(false);
      s.children.push(this.root);
      splitChild(s, 0, this.t);
      this.root = s;
    }
    this.insertNonFull(this.root, k);
  }
  insertNonFull(x: BNode, k: number): void {
    let i = x.keys.length - 1;
    while (i >= 0 && k < (x.keys[i] as number)) i--;
    if (x.leaf) {
      x.keys.splice(i + 1, 0, k);
      return;
    }
    i++;
    if ((x.children[i] as BNode).keys.length === 2 * this.t - 1) {
      splitChild(x, i, this.t);
      if (k > (x.keys[i] as number)) i++;
    }
    this.insertNonFull(x.children[i] as BNode, k);
  }
}
Complexity: O(t log_t n)

