Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · date · ordering · L2
Concept: Subtracting Dates is an error in TypeScript (TS2362, TS2363); subtract getTime() values in a comparator
Misconception: dates.sort((a, b) => a - b) works because dates convert to numbers.
Explanation: JavaScript allows it, but TypeScript rejects arithmetic on Date operands with TS2362 (left side) and TS2363 (right side). Subtract getTime() values. The default sort() converts to strings, which does not order dates correctly.
Incorrect (compile error TS2362, TS2363):
function sortBad(ds: Date[]): Date[] {
  return [...ds].sort((a, b) => a - b);
}
Correct:
function sortDates(ds: readonly Date[]): Date[] {
  return [...ds].sort((a, b) => a.getTime() - b.getTime());
}
Complexity: O(n log n)

