TypeScript · deque · mutation · L2
Concept: Rotate by k mod size, normalised for negative k
Misconception: Looping k times rotates correctly for any integer k.
Explanation: A negative k never runs the loop, so nothing rotates, and a huge k repeats full turns. Reduce first: steps = ((k % n) + n) % n, then move steps items from the back to the front.
Incorrect:
function rotateBad<T>(d: Deque<T>, k: number): void {
  for (let i = 0; i < k; i++) d.pushFront(d.popBack() as T);
}
Correct:
function rotate<T>(d: Deque<T>, k: number): void {
  const n = d.size;
  if (n === 0) return;
  const steps = ((k % n) + n) % n;
  for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) d.pushFront(d.popBack() as T);
}
Complexity: O(n)

