Concept: A directed edge is stored once, on the source vertex only
Misconception: addEdge(u, v) should also record v to u.
Explanation: In a directed graph the edge u to v does not imply v to u. Adding both directions turns the graph into an undirected one: cycle detection, topological order and strongly connected components all give wrong answers. Store the edge only in adj[u].
