Concept: Bit-flag enums combine with |, and a combined value must be tested with & rather than ===
Misconception: p === Perm.Write is true whenever the Write permission is among the flags.
Explanation: Powers of two let one number hold several flags: Read | Write is 3. Equality with a single flag is false for any combination. Test a flag with (p & flag) === flag, add with |, and remove with & ~flag.
Incorrect:
function hasBad(p: number, flag: number): boolean {
  return p === flag;
}
Correct:
enum Perm { Read = 1, Write = 2, Exec = 4 }
function has(p: Perm, flag: Perm): boolean {
  return (p & flag) === flag;
}
Complexity: O(1)

