Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · enum · access · L1
Concept: A numeric enum compiles to an object with reverse mappings, so Object.keys lists the numbers too
Misconception: Object.keys(Color) returns only the member names.
Explanation: For a numeric enum TypeScript emits both Color.Red = 0 and Color[0] = "Red". Object.keys, Object.values and for...in therefore see twice as many entries. Filter out the numeric keys, or use a string enum or an as const object, which have no reverse mapping.
Incorrect:
enum ColorB { Red, Green }
function namesBad(): string[] {
  return Object.keys(ColorB);
}
Correct:
enum Color { Red, Green }
function names(): string[] {
  return Object.keys(Color).filter((k) => Number.isNaN(Number(k)));
}
Complexity: O(n)

