Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · fenwicktree · access · L2
Concept: The tree is 1-based internally, so a 0-based index must be shifted by one before walking
Misconception: Start a query at x = i for a 0-based index i.
Explanation: Index 0 has no lowest set bit, so a 1-based tree cannot store it. Public methods take a 0-based index and shift it with x = i + 1. Starting a query at i leaves out element i, and an update starting at i = 0 would loop forever because x & -x is 0.
Incorrect:
function prefixBad(tree: number[], i: number): number {
  let sum = 0;
  for (let x = i; x > 0; x -= x & -x) sum += tree[x] as number;
  return sum;
}
Correct:
function prefixSum(tree: number[], i: number): number {
  let sum = 0;
  for (let x = i + 1; x > 0; x -= x & -x) sum += tree[x] as number;
  return sum;
}
Complexity: O(log n)

