Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · hashtable · insertion-and-deletion · L2
Concept: Delete removes one entry from its chain; clearing the chain removes the colliding keys too
Misconception: Emptying the bucket removes the key.
Explanation: The bucket may contain other keys that collided with it. Clearing the whole chain deletes them silently. Find the entry index with findIndex and splice that one entry, then decrement the count.
Incorrect:
function delBad<V>(t: Table<string | number, V>, k: string | number): void {
  const chain = t.buckets[indexOf(k, t.buckets.length)] as [string | number, V][];
  if (chain.some(([key]) => sameKey(key, k))) {
    t.count -= chain.length;
    chain.length = 0;
  }
}
Correct:
function del<V>(t: Table<string | number, V>, k: string | number): boolean {
  const chain = t.buckets[indexOf(k, t.buckets.length)] as [string | number, V][];
  const i = chain.findIndex(([key]) => sameKey(key, k));
  if (i < 0) return false;
  chain.splice(i, 1);
  t.count--;
  return true;
}
Complexity: O(1) average

