Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · hashtable · insertion-and-deletion · L2
Concept: Resizing must rehash every key: the bucket index depends on the capacity
Misconception: Copying the old buckets into a larger array keeps lookups working.
Explanation: The index is hash % capacity, so a different capacity maps keys to different buckets. Copying old buckets as they are leaves keys where lookup will not look. Create the new bucket array and insert every entry again. Doubling the capacity when the load factor passes about 0.75 keeps chains short and makes insertion amortised O(1).
Incorrect:
function resizeBad<V>(t: Table<string | number, V>, cap: number): void {
  const old = t.buckets;
  t.buckets = Array.from({ length: cap }, (_, i) => old[i] ?? []);
}
Correct:
function resize<V>(t: Table<string | number, V>, cap: number): void {
  const old = t.buckets;
  t.buckets = Array.from({ length: cap }, () => [] as [string | number, V][]);
  for (const chain of old) {
    for (const entry of chain) t.buckets[indexOf(entry[0], cap)]!.push(entry);
  }
}
Complexity: O(n)

