TypeScript · heap · testing · L2
Concept: Check the heap invariant for every parent-child pair, not only the left child
Misconception: Comparing each parent with its left child is enough to validate a heap.
Explanation: The invariant is that every parent is not larger than either child (for a min-heap). A check that tests only the left child accepts arrays where the right child is smaller. Loop over all indexes i > 0 and compare with parent (i - 1) >> 1.
Incorrect:
function isMinHeapBad(a: number[]): boolean {
  for (let i = 0; 2 * i + 1 < a.length; i++) {
    if ((a[i] as number) > (a[2 * i + 1] as number)) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
Correct:
function isMinHeap(a: number[]): boolean {
  for (let i = 1; i < a.length; i++) {
    if ((a[(i - 1) >> 1] as number) > (a[i] as number)) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
Complexity: O(n)

