TypeScript · interface · testing · L2
Concept: Interfaces are erased: instanceof with an interface is error TS2693; test shapes with a type guard
Misconception: x instanceof Shape works when Shape is an interface.
Explanation: An interface exists only at compile time, so there is nothing to compare against at run time. Using it as a value is error TS2693. Write a type guard function that checks the properties or a discriminant field, or use a class when instanceof is required.
Incorrect (compile error TS2693):
interface ShapeB { area(): number }
function isShapeBad(x: unknown): boolean {
  return x instanceof ShapeB;
}
Correct:
interface Shape { area(): number }
function isShape(x: unknown): x is Shape {
  return typeof x === "object" && x !== null && typeof (x as Shape).area === "function";
}
Complexity: O(1)

