TypeScript · json · edge-cases · L2
Concept: JSON.stringify throws TypeError on a circular reference; track visited objects in a replacer
Misconception: JSON.stringify skips a reference it has already seen.
Explanation: A cycle makes stringify throw TypeError ("Converting circular structure to JSON"). Use a replacer with a WeakSet of ancestors seen so far and replace repeats with a marker, or remove the back-reference before serialising.
Incorrect:
function dumpBad(o: object): string {
  return JSON.stringify(o);
}
Correct:
function dump(o: object): string {
  const seen = new WeakSet<object>();
  return JSON.stringify(o, (_k, v) => {
    if (typeof v === "object" && v !== null) {
      if (seen.has(v)) return "[Circular]";
      seen.add(v);
    }
    return v;
  });
}
Complexity: O(n)

