TypeScript · json · transformation · L1
Concept: A JSON round trip drops undefined and functions, turns NaN into null and Dates into strings; use structuredClone to copy
Misconception: JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x)) is a faithful deep copy.
Explanation: JSON has no undefined, function, symbol, NaN, Infinity, Date, Map or Set. Properties holding undefined or functions are dropped, NaN and Infinity become null, a Date becomes an ISO string, and Map and Set become {}. structuredClone copies those values correctly (but not functions).
Incorrect:
function cloneBad<T>(x: T): T {
  return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x));
}
Correct:
function clone<T>(x: T): T {
  return structuredClone(x);
}
Complexity: O(n)

