TypeScript · json · patterns · L3
Concept: Define toJSON on a class to choose exactly which fields are serialised
Misconception: JSON.stringify includes only the fields that are public in the TypeScript class.
Explanation: TypeScript visibility (private, protected) is erased, so every own enumerable property is serialised, including a password. If a value has a toJSON method, stringify calls it and serialises the result instead. Return a plain object with only the safe fields.
Incorrect:
class UserBad {
  constructor(public name: string, private password: string) {}
}
Correct:
class User {
  constructor(public name: string, private password: string) {}
  toJSON(): { name: string } {
    return { name: this.name };
  }
}
Complexity: O(1)

