TypeScript · linkedlist · patterns · L2
Concept: Slow and fast pointers find the middle; the loop condition decides which middle an even list returns
Misconception: Stopping when fast.next is null returns the second middle of an even list.
Explanation: The slow pointer moves one step while fast moves two. For [1, 2, 3, 4] the loop condition fast && fast.next ends with slow on 3 (second middle). The condition fast.next && fast.next.next ends on 2 (first middle). Decide which middle the problem wants before writing the condition.
Incorrect:
