Concept: Map compares object keys by reference, so a new object with the same fields is a different key
Misconception: m.get({ id: 1 }) finds the entry stored under another { id: 1 } object.
Explanation: Map uses SameValueZero: primitives compare by value, objects by identity. A fresh literal is a new object and never matches. Key the map by a primitive that identifies the object (an id or a joined string), or keep a reference to the original key object.
