TypeScript · record · iteration · L2
Concept: Object.entries gives [string, V][], so indexing another Record with the key is error TS7053
Misconception: Object.entries(rec) returns keys typed as the Record key union.
Explanation: The key in Object.entries is string, because an object may have extra keys. Using it to index a Record<"a" | "b", V> is error TS7053. Cast once (k as keyof typeof table) when you control the object, or iterate over a constant key list.
Incorrect (compile error TS7053):
const table: Record<"a" | "b", number> = { a: 1, b: 2 };
function sumBad(r: Record<string, number>): number {
  return Object.entries(r).reduce((t, [k, v]) => t + v * table[k], 0);
}
Correct:
const table2: Record<"a" | "b", number> = { a: 1, b: 2 };
function sum(r: Record<string, number>): number {
  return Object.entries(r).reduce((t, [k, v]) => t + v * (table2[k as "a" | "b"] ?? 0), 0);
}
Complexity: O(n)

