Concept: Object.fromEntries returns { [k: string]: V }, which is not a Record over a union; cast or build explicitly
Misconception: Object.fromEntries produces a Record with the exact key union.
Explanation: The result type is { [k: string]: V }, so assigning it to Record<"a" | "b", V> is error TS2739 (missing properties). Cast after you know all keys are present, or build the record with a typed loop that checks every key.
