TypeScript · record · mutation · L2
Concept: Readonly<Record<K, V>> blocks assignment at compile time (TS2540); Object.freeze enforces it at run time
Misconception: Readonly<Record<K, V>> makes the object immutable.
Explanation: Assigning to a key of a readonly record is error TS2540. The protection is compile-time only, so a cast or untyped code can still change it. Freeze the object for run-time safety, and note that freeze is shallow.
Incorrect (compile error TS2540):
function setBad(r: Readonly<Record<"a", number>>): void {
  r.a = 2;
}
Correct:
function lock(r: Record<"a", number>): Readonly<Record<"a", number>> {
  return Object.freeze({ ...r });
}
Complexity: O(1)

