TypeScript · regexp · creation · L1
Concept: Escape user text before building a RegExp, or characters such as . and ( change the meaning
Misconception: new RegExp(userText) searches for userText literally.
Explanation: The string is parsed as a pattern, so "a.b" also matches "axb" and "(" throws SyntaxError. Escape the special characters with replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&") before constructing the regex, or avoid the regex and use includes.
Incorrect:
function containsBad(hay: string, needle: string): boolean {
  return new RegExp(needle).test(hay);
}
Correct:
function escapeRe(s: string): string {
  return s.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&");
}
function contains(hay: string, needle: string): boolean {
  return new RegExp(escapeRe(needle)).test(hay);
}
Complexity: O(n)

