Concept: The bottom-up query takes a half-open range, so an inclusive end needs + 1
Misconception: query(l, r) includes the element at r.
Explanation: The iterative bottom-up loop runs while l < r, so the range is [l, r) and element r is excluded. A caller who thinks in inclusive ranges loses the last element. Convert at the boundary with r + 1, in one wrapper, so the rest of the code uses one convention.
