Concept: Claim a slot with compareExchange; checking a value and then writing it lets two threads both win
Misconception: if (i[k] === 0) { i[k] = 1 } is a safe way to claim a slot.
Explanation: Another thread can write between the check and the write, so both threads think they claimed the slot. Atomics.compareExchange(i, k, 0, 1) compares and writes as one step and returns the old value; the caller owns the slot only when the old value was 0.
Incorrect:
function claimBad(i: Int32Array, k: number): boolean {
  if (i[k] === 0) {
    i[k] = 1;
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
Correct:
function claim(i: Int32Array, k: number): boolean {
  return Atomics.compareExchange(i, k, 0, 1) === 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

