Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · sharedarraybuffer · insertion-and-deletion · L2
Concept: A growable SharedArrayBuffer can only grow, never shrink; grow below the current size throws RangeError
Misconception: A growable SharedArrayBuffer can be resized to any size up to its maximum.
Explanation: grow(n) requires the buffer to be created with maxByteLength, and n must be at least the current byteLength and at most the maximum. Shrinking throws RangeError. Existing views with no fixed length follow the new size.
Incorrect:
function shrinkBad(sab: SharedArrayBuffer): void {
  sab.grow(4);
}
Correct:
function growShared(sab: SharedArrayBuffer, n: number): boolean {
  if (!sab.growable || n < sab.byteLength || n > sab.maxByteLength) return false;
  sab.grow(n);
  return true;
}
Complexity: O(1)

