TypeScript · stack · patterns · L2
Concept: In postfix evaluation the first value popped is the right operand
Misconception: For "3 1 -" pop a then b and compute a - b.
Explanation: Operands are pushed left to right, so the top of the stack is the right operand. Popping the right one first and the left one second gives left - right. Reversing them computes 1 - 3 and gets -2 instead of 2; the mistake only shows for subtraction and division.
Incorrect:
function rpnBad(tokens: string[]): number {
  const st: number[] = [];
  for (const t of tokens) {
    if (["+", "-", "*", "/"].includes(t)) {
      const a = st.pop() as number;
      const b = st.pop() as number;
      st.push(t === "+" ? a + b : t === "-" ? a - b : t === "*" ? a * b : a / b);
    } else st.push(Number(t));
  }
  return st[0] as number;
}
Correct:
function rpn(tokens: string[]): number {
  const st: number[] = [];
  for (const t of tokens) {
    if (["+", "-", "*", "/"].includes(t)) {
      const b = st.pop() as number;
      const a = st.pop() as number;
      st.push(t === "+" ? a + b : t === "-" ? a - b : t === "*" ? a * b : a / b);
    } else st.push(Number(t));
  }
  return st[0] as number;
}
Complexity: O(n)

