TypeScript · trie · patterns · L2
Concept: Autocomplete collects only nodes marked as word ends below the prefix node
Misconception: Every node below the prefix is a completion.
Explanation: Interior nodes are prefixes, not words. Collect the path only when the node is marked as a word end. Emitting at every node returns "ap" and "appl" as suggestions when only "app", "apple" and "apt" were inserted. Start from the node found for the prefix and return an empty list when it does not exist.
Incorrect:
function completeBad(t: Trie, prefix: string): string[] {
  const start = t.find(prefix);
  if (!start) return [];
  const out: string[] = [];
  const walk = (node: TrieNode, acc: string): void => {
    out.push(acc);
    for (const [ch, c] of node.children) walk(c, acc + ch);
  };
  walk(start, prefix);
  return out;
}
Correct:
function complete(t: Trie, prefix: string): string[] {
  const start = t.find(prefix);
  if (!start) return [];
  const out: string[] = [];
  const walk = (node: TrieNode, acc: string): void => {
    if (node.end) out.push(acc);
    for (const [ch, c] of node.children) walk(c, acc + ch);
  };
  walk(start, prefix);
  return out;
}
Complexity: O(P + output)

