Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · trie · insertion-and-deletion · L3
Concept: Delete clears the end flag and prunes nodes that no longer lead to any word
Misconception: Deleting a word only needs to clear its end flag.
Explanation: Clearing the flag makes has() correct but leaves the path in place, so startsWith still reports the prefix and memory is never freed. After clearing the flag, walk back up and remove each node that has no children and is not the end of another word, stopping at the first node that is still needed.
Incorrect:
function removeBad(t: Trie, word: string): boolean {
  const node = t.find(word);
  if (!node || !node.end) return false;
  node.end = false;
  return true;
}
Correct:
function remove(t: Trie, word: string): boolean {
  const path: Array<[TrieNode, string]> = [];
  let node = t.root;
  for (const ch of word) {
    const next = node.children.get(ch);
    if (!next) return false;
    path.push([node, ch]);
    node = next;
  }
  if (!node.end) return false;
  node.end = false;
  for (let i = path.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    const [parent, ch] = path[i] as [TrieNode, string];
    const child = parent.children.get(ch) as TrieNode;
    if (child.end || child.children.size > 0) break;
    parent.children.delete(ch);
  }
  return true;
}
Complexity: O(L)

