Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · trie · patterns · L3
Concept: The common prefix stops at the first branch or the first word end
Misconception: Follow single-child nodes to find the longest common prefix.
Explanation: A node with one child can still be the end of a stored word, such as "app" among "app" and "apple". The common prefix of all words stops there, because the short word has no more characters. Stop at a node that has several children, no child, or the end flag.
Incorrect:
function lcpBad(t: Trie): string {
  let node = t.root;
  let out = "";
  while (node.children.size === 1) {
    const [ch, next] = [...node.children][0] as [string, TrieNode];
    out += ch;
    node = next;
  }
  return out;
}
Correct:
function lcp(t: Trie): string {
  let node = t.root;
  let out = "";
  while (node.children.size === 1 && !node.end) {
    const [ch, next] = [...node.children][0] as [string, TrieNode];
    out += ch;
    node = next;
  }
  return out;
}
Complexity: O(L)

