Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · trie · patterns · L3
Concept: A wildcard search branches over all children at a dot instead of looking up the dot
Misconception: A pattern with "." can be searched with the normal has().
Explanation: The normal search follows one child per character, so "." is looked up as the literal character and never matches. At a dot the search must try every child and succeed if any branch matches the rest of the pattern. All other characters follow one child.
Incorrect:
function searchDotBad(t: Trie, pattern: string): boolean {
  return t.has(pattern);
}
Correct:
function searchDot(t: Trie, pattern: string): boolean {
  const go = (node: TrieNode, i: number): boolean => {
    if (i === pattern.length) return node.end;
    const ch = pattern[i] as string;
    if (ch === ".") {
      for (const c of node.children.values()) if (go(c, i + 1)) return true;
      return false;
    }
    const next = node.children.get(ch);
    return next !== undefined && go(next, i + 1);
  };
  return go(t.root, 0);
}
Complexity: O(26^d * L)

