Concept: Variadic tuple types let concat return [...A, ...B]; without them the result widens to an array
Misconception: Spreading two tuples into an array literal keeps their element types.
Explanation: Without an explicit return type, [...a, ...b] has type (A[number] | B[number])[], and assigning it to [number, string] is error TS2322. A generic function with A extends unknown[] and B extends unknown[] can return [...A, ...B], which keeps positions.
