TypeScript · typealias · edge-cases · L2
Concept: Intersecting two types with conflicting property types makes that property never; use Omit and add
Misconception: A & B with id: number and id: string lets id be either.
Explanation: An intersection requires every member to hold, so id: number & string is never and no value fits (error TS2322 on any assignment). To override a property, remove it first with Omit<A, "id"> and intersect with the new type.
