Concept: A mapped type can remove readonly with -readonly; without it the property cannot be assigned (TS2540)
Misconception: Readonly<T> can be undone by assigning to a copy typed as T.
Explanation: Mapped types rewrite every property: { -readonly [K in keyof T]: T[K] } removes readonly, and -? removes optionality. Assigning through a Readonly view is error TS2540. Define Mutable<T> and use it where mutation is intended.
