Imported reference; not locally executed. Subject: typescript
TypeScript · undirectedgraph · edge-cases · L2
Concept: The edge count is half the sum of degrees, with each self-loop added back once
Misconception: edges = sum of neighbour counts / 2.
Explanation: Each ordinary edge appears in two neighbour sets, so halving the sum works. A self-loop appears once in its own set, so the halved sum is fractional. Add the number of loops to the sum before halving, which counts each loop as degree two.
Incorrect:
function edgeCountBad(g: UGraph): number {
  let sum = 0;
  for (const s of g.adj) sum += s.size;
  return sum / 2;
}
Correct:
function edgeCount(g: UGraph): number {
  let sum = 0;
  let loops = 0;
  g.adj.forEach((s, u) => {
    sum += s.size;
    if (s.has(u)) loops++;
  });
  return (sum + loops) / 2;
}
Complexity: O(V)

