TypeScript · weakmap · equality · L1
Concept: A copy of an object is a different WeakMap key; the data stays with the original
Misconception: wm.get({ ...o }) finds the value stored for o.
Explanation: WeakMap matches keys by identity. A spread copy or structuredClone result is a new object, so the lookup misses. Pass the original reference, or store the data on the copy when you create it.
Incorrect:
function metaOfBad(wm: WeakMap<object, string>, o: { id: number }): string | undefined {
  return wm.get({ ...o });
}
Correct:
function metaOf(wm: WeakMap<object, string>, o: { id: number }): string | undefined {
  return wm.get(o);
}
Complexity: O(1)

