TypeScript · weakmap · mutation · L2
Concept: Keep private per-object data in a WeakMap instead of adding a property that shows up in keys and JSON
Misconception: Adding a hidden field to an object keeps it out of serialised output.
Explanation: A property added to an object is enumerable: it appears in Object.keys, spread copies and JSON.stringify, so it can leak. A module-level WeakMap keyed by the object stores the secret outside the object, is dropped with it when collected, and works on frozen objects.
Incorrect:
function setSecretBad<T extends object>(o: T, s: string): T {
  return Object.assign(o, { secret: s });
}
Correct:
const secrets = new WeakMap<object, string>();
function setSecret(o: object, s: string): void {
  secrets.set(o, s);
}
function getSecret(o: object): string | undefined {
  return secrets.get(o);
}
Complexity: O(1)

