TypeScript · weakset · testing · L3
Concept: A WeakSet of issued objects is an unforgeable brand check; a structural check can be faked
Misconception: Checking for an id property proves an object came from our factory.
Explanation: TypeScript is structural, so any object with the right fields passes a shape check. Record every object your factory creates in a module-level WeakSet and test membership: only real instances pass. This is the pattern behind private brand checks.
Incorrect:
function isTokenBad(x: unknown): boolean {
  return typeof x === "object" && x !== null && "id" in x;
}
Correct:
const issued = new WeakSet<object>();
function issue(id: number): { id: number } {
  const t = { id };
  issued.add(t);
  return t;
}
function isToken(x: unknown): boolean {
  return typeof x === "object" && x !== null && issued.has(x);
}
Complexity: O(1)

